hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4801","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from al-Dahhak ibn Nibras al-Jahdami from Thabit, who said: I was with Anas ibn Malik at al-Zawiya when he heard the adhan, so he dismounted and I dismounted with him; when he settled on the ground he walked with me, then shortened his steps until I entered the mosque, and he said: Do you know, O Thabit, why I walked with you in this manner until I entered the mosque? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked with me in this manner and said: Do you know why I walked with you in this manner? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: So that the number of steps in seeking the prayer may be numerous."
"4802","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba (H). And narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba - both said: narrated Abd Allah ibn Musa from al-Dahhak ibn Nibras from Thabit from Anas from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The iqama for the prayer was called, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, and I was with him, and he shortened his steps and said: I only did this so that the number of my steps in seeking the prayer may be numerous."
"4803","Narrated Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani from Harami ibn Umara from al-Dahhak ibn Nibras from Thabit al-Bunani from Anas ibn Malik from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were heading for the prayer, and he was shortening his steps, then he said: Do you know why I shorten my steps? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The servant remains in prayer so long as he is in pursuit of the prayer."
"4804","Narrated Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi from Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Bunani from his father from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I was walking with Zayd ibn Thabit to the mosque, and he shortened his steps, then said: Do you know why I walked with you in this manner? I said: No. He said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he shortened his steps and said: Do you know why I walked with you in this manner? I said: No. He said: So that our steps in walking to the prayer may be numerous."
"4805","Abu Hurayra from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati from Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri from Ibn Abi Hazim from Abd Allah ibn Amir from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him) from Zayd ibn Thabit from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah remains in the need of the servant so long as the servant is in the need of his brother."
"4806","Narrated Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati from Abu Nu'aym from Abd Allah ibn Amir al-Aslami from Abu al-Zinad from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah remains in the need of the servant so long as he is in the need of his brother."
"4807","Abu al-Darda from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti from Abu al-Mughira from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam from Damra ibn Habib from Abu al-Darda from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him this supplication and commanded him to learn it and to impress it upon his household every day, saying in the morning: At Your service, O Allah, at Your service, and happiness is in Your hands, and good is from You and through You and to You. O Allah, whatever word I utter, or oath I swear, or vow I vow, Your will stands before it; what You will is, and what You do not will is not; there is no power nor strength except through You; indeed You have power over all things. O Allah, whatever prayer I offer, it is upon whomever You have prayed upon, and whatever curse I utter, it is upon whomever You have cursed. You are my Guardian in this world and the Hereafter; cause me to die as a Muslim and join me with the righteous. O Allah, I ask You for contentment after the decree, and coolness of life after death, and the delight of gazing upon Your Noble Face, and longing to meet You, without harmful affliction or misleading tribulation. I seek refuge in You, O Allah, from wronging or being wronged, or transgressing or being transgressed against, or earning a mistaken sin or an unforgiven sin. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Possessor of Majesty and Honor, I pledge to You in this worldly life, and I call You to witness - and You suffice as a witness - that I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone without partner; to You belongs dominion and to You belongs praise, and You have power over all things; and I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger; and I bear witness that Your promise is true, and meeting You is true, and the Hour is coming with no doubt in it, and that You will resurrect those in the graves; and I bear witness that if You entrust me to myself, You entrust me to weakness, exposure, sin, defect, and error; and I place trust only in Your mercy. Forgive me all my sins, for none forgives sins but You, and turn to me in forgiveness, for indeed You are the Oft-Returning, the Merciful."
"4808","Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Sulayman ibn Harb and Amr ibn Marzuq, who said: narrated Shu'ba from Adi ibn Thabit from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Thabit say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Uhud, a group of people turned back on the way, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were split into two parties regarding them, one party saying: Accept them, and one party saying: Do not accept them. So Allah (Mighty and Majestic) sent down: What is the matter with you that you are two parties regarding the hypocrites, while Allah has cast them back for what they earned."
"4809","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth from al-Ashja'i from Sufyan from Jabir from Adi ibn Thabit from Abd Allah ibn Yazid from Zayd ibn Thabit regarding: What is the matter with you that you are two parties regarding the hypocrites. He said: The hypocrites and the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were in a house, and one group said: We wish they would come out to us so we could fight them, while another group disliked that until their voices rose; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said to Zayd: Write it: What is the matter with you that you are two parties regarding the hypocrites, while Allah has cast them back for what they earned."
"4810","Narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i al-Qadi from Ali ibn Nasr ibn Ali from Uthman ibn al-Yaman from Abd al-Samad ibn Sulayman, who said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me from Abd Allah ibn Yazid from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Zayd, give the zakat of your head along with the people, even if you find nothing but a sa' of wheat."
"4811","Adi ibn Umayra al-Kindi from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar from Ayyub from Adi ibn Adi from his father - or his uncle - that there was a slave called Kaysan, who named himself Qays, claimed kinship to his master, and joined Kufa. So his father rode to Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: O Commander of the Believers, my son was born on my bed, then he turned away from me and claimed kinship to his master and my master. Umar said to Zayd ibn Thabit: Do you not know that we used to recite: Do not turn away from your fathers, for it is disbelief in you. Zayd said: Yes. So Umar said to him: Go, join your son to your camel; go and strike your camel with a whip and your son with a whip until you bring him to your family."
"4812","Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Uthman ibn Uthman al-Ghatafani, who said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed me from al-Zuhri from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: I was with a group who differed about the middle prayer, and I was the youngest of the group, so they sent me to Zayd ibn Thabit to ask him about the middle prayer. He said: So I came to him and asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr at midday heat while people were in their siesta and their markets, and none would pray behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except one or two rows. So Allah (Mighty and Majestic) sent down: Guard strictly the prayers, and the middle prayer, and stand before Allah devoutly. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Certain people shall surely desist, or I shall surely burn their houses."
"4813","Narrated Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati from Abu Nu'aym from Abd Allah ibn Amir from Abu al-Zinad from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise; you say often: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"4814","Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Abu Mus'ab (H). And narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani - both said: narrated Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad from Yunus ibn Yusuf ibn Himas from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until they are safe from blight."
"4815","Marwan ibn al-Hakam from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulayka say: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Marwan ibn al-Hakam informed him, saying: Zayd ibn Thabit said to me: Why do you recite the short Mufassal chapters in the Maghrib prayer, when the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Maghrib prayer the long of the two long ones. I said to Urwa: And what is the long of the two long ones? He said: Al-A'raf."
"4816","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abu Asim from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abi Mulayka, who said: Urwa informed me from Marwan, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit said to me: Why do I see you reciting the short Mufassal in the prayer? I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting the two long ones. I said: And what are the two long ones? He said: Al-A'raf and Yunus."
"4817","Narrated Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas from his father from Ibn Wahb from Amr ibn al-Harith from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit said to Marwan ibn al-Hakam: You recite: Say, He is Allah, One and: Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar. He said: Yes. Then Zayd ibn Thabit said: By oath, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting the longer of the two long ones."
"4818","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi (H). And narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad - both said: narrated Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from al-Zuhri from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I entered the mosque and there was Marwan ibn al-Hakam sitting, so I sat beside him, and he informed us that Zayd ibn Thabit informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dictated to him: Those who sit back and those who strive are not equal. Then Ibn Umm Maktum said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, if I could strive I would strive. So Allah (Mighty and Majestic) sent down upon him, while his thigh was upon my thigh, and his thigh grew heavy upon me until my thigh was almost crushed; then it was lifted from him and he said: Except those with a disability."
"4819","Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti from Wahb ibn Baqiyya from Khalid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from al-Zuhri from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, the Companion of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Marwan ibn al-Hakam from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I was sitting beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my thigh beneath his thigh, while he was dictating to me: Those who sit back among the believers and those who strive in the path of Allah with their wealth and their lives are not equal - and Ibn Umm Maktum was sitting listening - and he said: By Allah, if I could strive I would strive, O Prophet of Allah. So Allah sent down the Quran upon His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his thigh grew heavy upon my thigh until I thought it would crush it; then it was lifted from him and he said: Those who sit back among the believers, except those with a disability, are not equal."
"4820","Narrated Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh from Ibrahim ibn Hamza al-Zubayri from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ibn Shihab from Sahl ibn Sa'd that he saw Marwan ibn al-Hakam sitting in the mosque, so I came until I sat beside him, and he informed us that Zayd ibn Thabit informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dictated to him: Those who sit back among the believers and those who strive in the path of Allah are not equal. Then Ibn Umm Maktum came to him while he was dictating it to me and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, if I could strive I would strive! And he was a blind man. So Allah (Mighty and Majestic) sent down upon His Messenger while his thigh was upon my thigh, and it grew heavy upon me until I thought it would crush my thigh; then it was lifted from him, and Allah (Mighty and Majestic) sent down: Except those with a disability."
"4821","Narrated Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi from Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulatha from Thawr ibn Yazid from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, who said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan narrating from his father from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: Sleeplessness afflicted me at night, so I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Say: O Allah, the stars have set, the eyes have grown still, and You are the Living, the Sustainer. O Living, O Sustainer, put my eye to sleep and calm my night. So I said it and it left me."
"4822","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi from al-Haytham ibn Jamil (H). And narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Sa'id ibn Sulayman - both said: narrated Yazid ibn Iyad from Isma'il ibn Abi Hakim from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan."
"4823","Narrated Abu al-Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd and al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan."
"4824","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd and al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sell fruit until its soundness becomes evident."
"4825","Urwa ibn al-Zubayr from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi from Amr ibn Marzuq from Shu'ba from Amr ibn Abi Hakim from al-Zibriqan from Urwa from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at midday heat - or he said: at midday - and it was the heaviest prayer upon his Companions, so there was sent down: Guard strictly the prayers, and the middle prayer, and stand before Allah devoutly. He said: Because before it are two prayers and after it are two prayers."
"4826","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal (H). And narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami and Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir, who said: narrated Yazid ibn Zuray' (H). And narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba (H). And narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, who said: narrated Ibn Ulayya - all of them from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from Abu Ubayda ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: May Allah forgive Rafi' ibn Khadij; by Allah, I knew the hadith better than him. Two men who had fought each other came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If this is your situation, then do not lease farmlands. So Rafi' heard his saying: Do not lease farmlands. The wording is that of the hadith of Musaddad."
"4827","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Waki' from Hisham ibn Urwa from Abu Ayyub or Zayd ibn Thabit that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in Maghrib al-A'raf in two rak'as."
"4828","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman from Uqba ibn Khalid from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rak'as of Maghrib Surat al-Anfal."
"4829","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Abu Kurayb from Firdaws ibn al-Ash'ari from Layth ibn Sa'd from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leading us in the Maghrib prayer with Alif-Lam-Mim-Sad until he reached its end."
"4830","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari from Muhammad ibn Musaffa from Uthman ibn Sa'id from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa from Zayd ibn Thabit from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Nothing of fruit is to be sold until its soundness becomes evident, and that is when the red blush becomes distinct from the yellow."
"4831","Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri from Yahya ibn Bukayr from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman from Urwa, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Thabit say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in Maghrib the longer of the two long ones."
"4832","Narrated Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj from Yusuf ibn Adi from Ali ibn Mushir from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit said: The mosque founded upon piety is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Urwa said: The mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is better than it; it was only sent down concerning the mosque of Quba."
"4833","Ata ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him). Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil and Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi, who said: narrated Ali ibn al-Ja'd from Ibn Abi Dhi'b from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt from Ata ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I recited before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) al-Najm and he did not prostrate."
"4834","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qa'nabi from Malik from Yunus ibn Yusuf from Ata ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Thabit al-Ansari that he found boys who had cornered a fox in a corner, so he drove them away from it. And Malik said: I only know that he said: Is this done in the sanctuary of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"4835","Narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi from Abu Hudhayfa from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad from Sharik ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir from Ata ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Thabit that he said before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What an evil thing is leadership! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What a good thing is leadership for whoever takes it with its right and its lawful due, and what an evil thing is leadership for whoever takes it without its right, for it will be a cause of regret for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"4836","Sulayman ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father (may Allah have mercy on him) from Muhammad ibn Ja'far from Shu'ba, who said: I heard Hadir ibn al-Muhajir Abu Isa al-Bahili say: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar narrating from Zayd ibn Thabit that a wolf wounded a sheep, so they slaughtered it with a sharp stone, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted eating it."
"4837","Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father; Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman from Kharija ibn Zayd. Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abu Asim from Ibn Abi Dhi'b from Ibn Shihab from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr from Kharija ibn Zayd from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from that which fire has altered (by cooking)."
"4838","Narrated Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi (H). And narrated Abu Zur'a al-Dimashqi - both said: narrated Abu al-Yaman from Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamza from al-Zuhri from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman from Kharija ibn Zayd from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from that which fire has touched."
"4839","Narrated Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi from Abd Allah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir, who said: Muhammad ibn Muslim said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me that Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit al-Ansari informed him that his father Zayd ibn Thabit said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from that which fire has touched."
"4840","Narrated Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi from Amr ibn Qust from Ubayd Allah ibn Amr from Ishaq ibn Rashid from al-Zuhri from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from that which fire has touched."
"4841","Narrated Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb from Abd Allah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Uqayl from Ibn Shihab that Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr informed him from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from that which fire has touched."
"4842","Narrated Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri from Ahmad ibn Salih from Anbasa ibn Khalid from Yunus ibn Yazid from Ibn Shihab: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me from Kharija ibn Zayd that Zayd ibn Thabit said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from that which fire has touched."
"4843","Narrated Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi from Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Ba'labakki from Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Awza'i from al-Zuhri from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from that which fire has touched."
"4844","Narrated al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi from Suwayd ibn Sa'id from al-Walid ibn Muslim al-Muwaqqari from al-Zuhri from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from that which fire has touched."
"4845","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami (H). And narrated Abu Husayn from Yahya al-Himmani - both said: narrated Yazid ibn Zuray' from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri from Kharija ibn Zayd from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from that which fire has touched. Abu al-Qasim said: Ma'mar did not mention Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr."
"4846","Narrated Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Khabayiri al-Himsi from Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abrash from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi from al-Zuhri from Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from that which fire has touched."
"4847","Al-Zuhri from Kharija ibn Zayd from Zayd. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri from Kharija ibn Zayd, who said: Zayd said: When we wrote the masahif I missed a verse which I used to hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I found it with Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari: Among the believers are men who were true to what they pledged to Allah; among them is one who fulfilled his vow, and among them is one who waits, and they did not change at all. He said: And Khuzayma was called Dhu al-Shahadatayn (the one of two testimonies)."
"4848","Narrated Abu Khalifa from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi (H). And narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani - both said: we heard Ibrahim ibn Sa'd say: Ibn Shihab said: Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit informed me, saying: He heard Zayd ibn Thabit say: I missed a verse from Surat al-Ahzab when I was copying the mushaf, and I used to hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting it, so I sought it and found it with Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari: Among the believers are men who were true to what they pledged to Allah. So I attached it in its sura in the mushaf."
"4849","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Khalid ibn Khidash from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi from Amr ibn Abi Amr from al-Zuhri from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: On the day of Yamama many of those who recited the Quran were struck down - he mentioned about four hundred - so I came to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said to him: If another battle occurs the Quran will be lost. Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I will not change anything which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do. So he sent for Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said the same: We will not change anything which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do. Zayd ibn Thabit said: I said: What is it to you (what harm)? They said: You are right. So Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) had it written on palm stalks and shoulder blades."
"4850","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i from my uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi from Umara ibn Ghaziyya from Ibn Shihab from Kharija ibn Zayd from his father, who said: Umar came to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both) and said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when they were killed on the day of Yamama, fell like moths fall - then he mentioned the hadith in full."
"4851","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar from al-Zuhri from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not sell fruit until the Pleiades rise and its soundness becomes evident."
"4852","Narrated Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Salih al-Marwazi al-Misri from Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami from Wuhayb from al-Nu'man ibn Rashid from al-Zuhri from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sell fruits until the Pleiades rise."
"4853","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi from Salama ibn al-Fadl from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from al-Zuhri from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sell fruit until its soundness becomes evident."
"4854","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from Amr ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tariq from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Yunus ibn Yazid from al-Zuhri from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the sale of araya (unripe dates on trees for harvested dates) in exchange for dates and fresh dates."
"4855","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani from Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat al-Razi from Abu al-Haytham Khalid ibn al-Qasim from Yunus ibn Yazid from al-Zuhri from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father that he used to say when he lay down: O Allah, I ask You for the sufficiency of family and master, and I seek refuge in You from a kinship tie I have severed invoking against me."
"4856","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib from Abd Allah ibn Musa al-Taymi from Usama ibn Zayd from al-Zuhri from Kharija ibn Zayd - I do not know whether he mentioned his father or not - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the sale of araya in exchange for dates and fresh dates."
"4857","Abu al-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi from Adam ibn Abi Iyas (H). And narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf, who said: narrated Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam (H). And narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani - all said: narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from my father Abu al-Zinad that Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to him from his father that stillness (sakina) came over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Zayd said: And I was beside him - so the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell upon my thigh, and I never found anything heavier than the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then it was lifted from him and he said: Write. So I wrote: Those who sit back among the believers and those who strive in the path of Allah with their wealth and their lives are not equal - the whole verses. He said: So I wrote that on a shoulder blade. Then Ibn Umm Maktum stood - and he was a blind man - when he heard the superiority of the strivers over those who sit back, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what about one among the believers who cannot strive? No sooner had Ibn Umm Maktum finished his speech - or he said: except that he complete his speech - than stillness came over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his thigh fell upon my thigh, and I felt from its weight the second time as I had felt the first time. Then it was lifted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Recite. So I recited: Those who sit back among the believers are not equal. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except those with a disability. Zayd said: So I attached it, and it is as if I am looking at its attachment beside a crack in the shoulder blade."
"4858","Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiya from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and stillness covered him - or revelation descended - so the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell upon my thigh, and I never saw anything settle heavier than the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When it was lifted - or relieved - from him, he said: Recite. So I recited. He said: Write: Those who sit back among the believers and those who strive in the path of Allah are not equal. Then Amr ibn Umm Maktum, the blind, said: O Messenger of Allah, my eyes are impaired. So stillness covered him, and the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell upon my thigh, and I never found anything at all heavier than the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When it was lifted - or relieved - from him, he said: Recite. So I recited. He said: Write: Except those with a disability. I never forgot its attachment beside a crack in the shoulder blade."
"4859","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf, who said: narrated Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Ibn Abi al-Zinad and Sufyan ibn Uyayna, who said: narrated Abu al-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from Zayd ibn Thabit regarding the saying of Allah (Mighty and Majestic): A mosque founded upon piety. He said: The mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4860","Narrated Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani from Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri from Ibn Abi Hazim from Abd Allah ibn Amir from Abu al-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the mosque founded upon piety: It is this mosque of mine."
"4861","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam (H). And narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Sa'id ibn Mansur (H). And narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Isa ibn Mina Qalun - all said: narrated Ibn Abi al-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: Recitation (according to the established reading) is sunna. Ibn Abi Maryam added: Do not oppose the people with your opinion."
"4862","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf, who said: narrated Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Ibn Abi al-Zinad: my father informed me from Kharija from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to learn the writing of the Jews. He said: So I used to write for him and write to them, and read for him when they wrote."
"4863","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to learn the writing of the Jews, and half a month did not pass before I had mastered it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not trust the Jews with my writing. So when I learned it, I used to write for him."
"4864","Narrated Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratis i and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf, who said: narrated Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam, who said: one whom I trust narrated to me from Ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina while I was eleven years old."
"4865","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim (H). And narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti from Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh, who said: narrated Ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the sale of araya to be sold by measure according to its estimate."
"4866","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf, who said: narrated Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Ibn Abi al-Zinad: my father narrated to me that he took this letter from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. To Abd Allah Mu'awiya, Commander of the Believers, from Zayd ibn Thabit: Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Believers, and the mercy of Allah. I praise Allah to you, besides whom there is no god. Now, you wrote asking me about the inheritance of the grandfather and brothers, and indeed kalala and much of what is decreed in these inheritances - none knows its extent but Allah. We used to attend such matters with the caliphs after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we retained of them what we wished to retain, so we give fatwa with it thereafter to whoever seeks fatwa from us regarding inheritances."
"4867","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn al-Mughira from al-Nu'man ibn Abd al-Salam from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina while they were trading fruits before they ripened, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard clamour and a loud sound from the people, so he said: What is this? They said: O Messenger of Allah, these are people who traded fruits on the palms, then they mentioned that blight struck them after that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then do not trade until they ripen."
"4868","Narrated Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Anbar al-Basri from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami from Abu Ghaziyya Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qadi al-Ansari from Ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ghusl for his ihram where he entered ihram."
"4869","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Abu Usama from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, Banu al-Najjar came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, among us is a boy who has recited some ten-odd suras of what was sent down upon you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and I recited to him."
"4870","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi from Ahmad ibn Zur'a from Abu Ghaziyya from Ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from Zayd ibn Thabit from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When boundaries are fixed, there is no pre-emption."
"4871","Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari from Ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father that he used to keep alive the night of the twenty-third of Ramadan and the night of the twenty-seventh, but not like his keeping alive the night of the seventeenth. So it was said to him: Why do you single out the night of the seventeenth? He said: In it the Quran was sent down, and on its morning truth was separated from falsehood, and in it he would wake with a radiant face."
"4872","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih and Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri, who said: narrated Fadala ibn al-Mufaddal ibn Fadala from my father from Muhammad ibn Ajlan from Abu al-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deception."
"4873","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Sa'id al-Musahiqi from Malik ibn Anas from Abu al-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted two shares for the horse and one share for the man."
"4874","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, who said: narrated Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan from Abbad ibn Abbad from Muhammad ibn Amr from Musa ibn Uqba from Abu al-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: This verse in Surat al-Nisa: Whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein, and Allah is angry with him and has cursed him and prepared for him a great punishment - was sent down six months after the verses in Surat al-Furqan: And those who do not invoke another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery; and whoever does that shall meet punishment."
"4875","Narrated Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri from Yahya ibn Bukayr from al-Layth ibn Sa'd from Khalid ibn Yazid from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal from Jahm ibn Abi Jahm that Abu al-Zinad informed them that Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit informed him from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: When this verse in al-Furqan was sent down: And those who do not invoke another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right - we marvelled at its leniency. So we remained seven months, then the one in al-Nisa was sent down: Whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein, and Allah is angry with him and has cursed him - until he finished."
"4876","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba and Abu Kurayb, who said: narrated Mu'awiya ibn Hisham from Khalid ibn Ilyas from Abd Allah ibn Dhakwan Abu al-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade blowing in prostration and blowing into drink."
"4877","Narrated Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shawdhab al-Wasiti from Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri from Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad from his brother from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit that Marwan said to Zayd ibn Thabit: O Abu Sa'id, if only you would leave us to write down your hadith from you. Zayd said: No. So Marwan seated a scribe behind the dome for him; he would question Zayd while the scribe wrote what Zayd narrated. He said: O Abu Sa'id, it seems we have obtained what you refused. He said: By Allah, I shall not move until I am brought it. So the book was brought and he tore it up and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to write his hadith."
"4878","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from my uncle Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh from my father from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This wealth is green and sweet."
"4879","Narrated Abu Zur'a Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi from Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This wealth is green and sweet."
"4880","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Asbahani from Yunus ibn Habib from Abu Dawud from Ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This wealth is green and sweet."
"4881","Narrated Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi from my father from my grandfather Khalid ibn Hayyan from Ali ibn Urwa from Yunus ibn Zayd from Abu al-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I saw a man ask my father about a man who fights in battle while buying, selling, and trading during his campaign. My father said to him: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Tabuk, buying and selling while he saw us and did not forbid us."
"4882","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jawari al-Wasiti from Zayd ibn Akhram from Abu Amir al-Aqadi from Ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd from his father, who said: The day of Ashura is not the day people speak of; it was only a day on which the Ka'ba was covered and the Abyssinians performed their spear-dance before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it would rotate through the year. People would come to a certain Jew and ask him, and when the Jew died they came to Zayd ibn Thabit and asked him."
"4883","Narrated Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yahya al-Adawi from Malik from Abu al-Zinad from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father, who said: A man from the Arabs came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him for land between two mountains, so he wrote it for him. Then he became Muslim, then he came to his people and said to them: Become Muslim, for I have come to you from a man who gives the giving of one who does not fear poverty."
"4884","Amr ibn Wahb from Kharija ibn Zayd. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri (H). And narrated Sulayman ibn Hasan al-Attar from Abu Kamil al-Jahdari - both said: narrated Abu Umayya ibn Ya'la from Abu al-Zinad from Amr ibn Wahb from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed only three rulings concerning the amma (skull wound exposing the membrane), the munaqqila (bone-displacing wound), and the mud iha (wound exposing the bone): for the amma thirty-three, for the munaqqila fifteen, and for the mudiha five; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed for the eye of a beast a quarter of its price."
"4885","Salim Abu al-Nadr from Kharija ibn Zayd. Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from my father from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Nadr from Kharija ibn Zayd from his father that when Uthman ibn Maz'un was buried, Umm al-Ala said: Be glad, O Abu al-Saib, you are in Paradise. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard her and said: Who is this? She said: It is I, O Prophet of Allah. He said: And what makes you know? She said: O Messenger of Allah, Uthman ibn Maz'un - he said: Indeed, we saw nothing but good; I am the Messenger of Allah, yet by Allah I do not know what will be done with me."
"4886","Qays ibn Sa'd ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from Kharija ibn Zayd. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Irs al-Marwazi al-Misri from Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Madini from Isma'il ibn Qays from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is forbidden."
"4887","Narrated Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar al-Wasiti from Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari from Uthman ibn Khalid al-Uthmani from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Wahb, the freedman of Zayd ibn Thabit, from his father from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no emigrant between Uthman and Ruqayya and Lut; meaning that they were the first to emigrate to the land of Abyssinia."
"4888","Sulayman ibn Kharija from Kharija ibn Zayd. Narrated Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi from Abd Allah ibn Salih from al-Layth from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid from Sulayman ibn Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit that he said: A group entered upon Zayd ibn Thabit and said: Narrate to us some of the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What shall I narrate to you? I was his neighbour; when revelation came down he would send for me and I would write the revelation, and when we mentioned the Hereafter he would mention it with us, and when we mentioned this world he would mention it with us, and when we mentioned food he would mention it with us. All of this I narrate to you from him."
"4889","Sa'id ibn Yasar from Kharija ibn Zayd. Narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib from Abu Sadaqa al-Juddi from Abd Allah ibn Amir al-Ansari then al-Aslami from Abu al-Zinad from Sa'id ibn Yasar from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"4890","Sa'id ibn Sulayman from Kharija ibn Zayd. Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Abu Musa al-Ansari from Anas ibn Iyad from Abd Allah ibn Amir from Abu al-Zinad from Sa'id ibn Sulayman of the family of Zayd ibn Thabit from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? They said: Yes. He said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"4891","Narrated Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati from Abu Nu'aym from Abd Allah ibn Amir al-Aslami from Abu al-Zinad from Sa'id ibn Sulayman from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise: There is no power nor strength except through Allah. And Abu Nu'aym did not mention Kharija."
"4892","Kathir ibn Zayd from Kharija ibn Zayd. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Abu Bakr al-Hanafi from Kathir ibn Zayd from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit: Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to prolong the recitation in Zuhr and Asr and move his lips, and I knew he only moved the lips for recitation."
"4893","Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father. Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Farwa ibn Abd Allah ibn Salama al-Ansari at al-Abwa from Harun ibn Yahya al-Hatibi from Zakariyya ibn Isma'il ibn Ya'qub ibn Isma'il ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father Isma'il from his uncle Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit said: One morning we went out early with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we were at a meeting of the roads of Medina, when we saw a Bedouin holding his camel's halter until he stopped before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were around him. He said: Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned the greeting to him and said: How are you this morning? He said: And the camel bellowed, and a man who looked like a guard came and the guard said: O Messenger of Allah, this Bedouin stole the camel. Then the camel bellowed for a while and grumbled, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) listened attentively, hearing its bellowing and grumbling. When the camel calmed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to the guard and said: Turn away from him, for the camel has testified against you that you are lying. So the guard turned away, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to the Bedouin and said: What did you say when you came to me? He said: I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad until no blessing remains; O Allah, bless Muhammad until no blessing remains; O Allah, grant peace to Muhammad until no peace remains; O Allah, have mercy upon Muhammad until no mercy remains. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, displayed it to me while the camel speaks its excuse, and the angels have filled the horizon."
"4894","Narrated Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim Duhaym from Abd Allah ibn Yahya al-Ma'afiri from Nafi' ibn Yazid from Uqayl ibn Khalid from al-Zuhri from Ibn Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit from his father from his grandfather Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I used to write the revelation with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his breathing would grow intense and he would sweat a heavy sweat like pearls, then he would be relieved. So I would write while he dictated to me, and I would not finish until it grew heavy - and when he finished he said: Recite. So I recited to him, and if there was an omission he would correct it."
"4895","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi' al-Tahhan al-Misri from Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, who said: I found in the book of my maternal uncle Abd al-Hamid: Uqayl narrated to me from Sa'id ibn Sulayman, who informed him from his father Sulayman ibn Zayd from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I used to write the revelation for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when it came down upon him he would be seized by intense distress and sweat a heavy sweat like pearls, then he would be relieved. So I would enter upon him with a piece of saddle-wood or a fragment and write while he dictated to me, and I would not finish until my leg almost broke from the weight of the Quran, so that I would say: I shall never walk on my leg again. When he finished he said: Recite it. If there was an omission in it he would correct it, then I would go out with it to the people."
"4896","Aban ibn Uthman ibn Affan from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Amr ibn Marzuq from Shu'ba, who said: I heard Umar ibn Sulayman narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aban ibn Uthman from his father from Zayd ibn Thabit from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: May Allah brighten a man who hears a hadith from us, memorises it, and conveys it; for many a carrier of understanding is not himself understanding. Three things over which the heart of a Muslim never harbours malice: sincerity of deed for Allah, sincere counsel to those in authority, and adherence to the community, for their supplication encompasses those behind them."
"4897","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Amr ibn Marzuq from Shu'ba, who said: I heard Umar ibn Sulayman narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aban ibn Uthman from his father from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has the Hereafter as his intention, Allah gathers his affairs for him, places his sufficiency in his heart, and the world comes to him submissive; and whoever has this world as his intention, Allah scatters his affairs, places his poverty before his eyes, and nothing of this world comes to him except what Allah has written for him. And Zayd ibn Thabit was asked about the middle prayer. He said: It is Asr."
"4898","Busr ibn Sa'id from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi from Abd al-Aziz ibn Mukhtar from Musa ibn Uqba from Salim Abu al-Nadr from Busr ibn Sa'id from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) partitioned a room - he thought - with a mat, and prayed in it. Some people heard of that, and some of them began to clear their throats, so he came out to them and said: What I have seen of your doing has continued with you until I feared it would be made obligatory upon you; had it been made obligatory upon you, you would not have upheld it. So pray, O people, in your houses, for the best prayer of a person is in his house except the prescribed prayer."
"4899","Narrated Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani and Ali ibn Jabala al-Asbahani and Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh, who said: narrated Isma'il ibn Abi Uways from Sulayman ibn Bilal from Ibrahim Bardan ibn Abi al-Nadr, the freedman of Umar ibn Ubayd Allah, from his father from Busr ibn Sa'id from Zayd ibn Thabit from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The prayer of a person in his house is better than his prayer in my mosque except the prescribed prayer."
"4900","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad from Bardan ibn Abi al-Nadr from his father from Busr ibn Sa'id from Zayd ibn Thabit from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the same."
"4901","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman from al-Muharibi from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind from Salim Abu al-Nadr from Busr ibn Sa'id from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) partitioned a room in the mosque and used to pray in it. A man saw him and they prayed with his prayer, until one night they attended while he did not come out to them, so they cleared their throats, pelted the door, and raised their voices. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them angry and said: O people, your doing has continued with you until I thought it would be prescribed; so upon you is prayer in your houses, for the best prayer of a person is in his house except the prescribed prayer."
"4902","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Waki' from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind from Salim Abu al-Nadr from Busr ibn Sa'id from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) partitioned a room and used to pray in it. His Companions noticed him and used to pray with his prayer. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best prayer is the prayer of a man in his house except the prescribed prayer."
"4903","Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Jahm al-Simmari from Azhar ibn Jamil from Hatim ibn Wardan from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from al-Zuhri from Amir ibn Sa'd from Zayd ibn Thabit from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If you hear of plague in a land, do not enter it; and if it occurs while you are in a land in which it is, do not leave it."
"4904","Kathir ibn Aflah from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar from Uthman ibn Umar (H). And narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Uthman ibn Umar from Hisham ibn Hassan (H). And narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Hudba ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Marwazi from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl from Hisham ibn Hassan from Ibn Sirin from Kathir ibn Aflah from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: We were commanded to glorify Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, praise thirty-three times, and magnify thirty-four times. Then a man from the Ansar saw in a dream-vision that one sees in sleep, and said: Did your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) command you to glorify so-and-so, praise so-and-so, and magnify so-and-so? He said: Yes. He said: Make them twenty-five and add the tahlil (there is no god but Allah) to them. So the Ansari came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of his dream, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make them as he said."
"4905","Qabisa ibn Dhuayb al-Khuza'i from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar (H). And narrated Musa ibn Jumhur al-Tinnisi al-Simsar from Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi from Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri from Qabisa ibn Dhuayb from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I used to write for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: Write: Those who sit back among the believers and those who strive in the path of Allah are not equal. Then Abd Allah ibn Umm Maktum came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I love striving in the path of Allah, but I have the affliction you see; my sight is gone! Zayd ibn Thabit said: Then the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grew heavy upon my thigh until I feared it would crush it. Then he said: Those who sit back among the believers, except those with a disability, and those who strive in the path of Allah are not equal."
"4906","Narrated Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani from Muhammad ibn Mu'awiya al-Naysaburi from Ibn Lahi'a from Abd Allah ibn Hubayra from Qabisa ibn Dhuayb from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Asr."
"4907","Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi from Abd Allah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir from Ibn Shihab from Ibn al-Sabbaq that Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to him, saying: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) sent for me at the time of the slaughter of the people of Yamama, and Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was with him. Abu Bakr said: Umar came to me and said to me: Slaughter has raged among the reciters of the Muslims at Yamama, and I fear slaughter will rage among the reciters in other places, and much of the Quran will go unpreserved; and I consider that you should command the collection of the Quran. I said to Umar: How can I do something which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? Umar said: By Allah, it is good. He kept returning to me about that until Allah expanded my chest for it, and I saw in it what Umar saw. Then he said to Zayd ibn Thabit, while Umar sat beside him without speaking: You are a young man whom I do not suspect, and you used to write the revelation for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so pursue the Quran and collect it. Zayd said: By Allah, had they charged me with moving a mountain from the mountains, it would not have been heavier upon me than what he commanded me of collecting the Quran. I said: How can you do something which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? He said: By Allah, it is good. Abu Bakr kept returning to me until Allah expanded my chest for what He had expanded the chests of Abu Bakr and Umar for. So I stood and pursued the Quran, collecting it from palm-leaf stalks, shoulder blades, saddle-wood pieces, palm branches, and the chests of men, until I found the end of Surat al-Tawba with Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari; I did not find it with anyone besides him: There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves. And the sheets were with Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) during his life until Allah took him, then with Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) until Allah took him, then with Hafsa bint Umar until Uthman collected the Quran from them into the masahif."
"4908","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri from Abd Allah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Yunus from Ibn Shihab: Ibn al-Sabbaq informed me that Zayd ibn Thabit said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) sent for me at the time of the slaughter of the people of Yamama, and Umar ibn al-Khattab was with him. Abu Bakr said: This man came to me and said to me: Slaughter has raged among the reciters of the Muslims at Yamama, and I fear slaughter will rage among the reciters in other places, and much of the Quran will go unpreserved; and I consider that you should command the collection of the Quran. I said to Umar: How can I do something which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? Umar said: By Allah, it is good. He kept returning to me about that until Allah expanded my chest for it, and I saw in it what Umar saw - while Umar sat beside him without speaking. Abu Bakr said: You are a young, intelligent man, and we do not suspect you, and you used to write the revelation for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so pursue the Quran and collect it. Zayd said: By Allah, had he charged me with moving a mountain from the mountains, it would not have been heavier upon me than what he commanded me of collecting the Quran. He said: I said: How can you do something which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? He said: By Allah, it is good. Abu Bakr kept returning to me until Allah expanded my chest for what He had expanded the chests of Abu Bakr and Umar for. He said: So I stood and pursued the Quran, collecting it from palm-leaf stalks, shoulder blades, saddle-wood pieces, palm branches, and the chests of men, until I found the last of Surat al-Tawba - two verses - with Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari; I did not find them with anyone besides him: There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves. And the sheets in which I collected the Quran were with Abu Bakr during his life until Allah took him, then with Umar until Allah took him, then with Hafsa bint Umar."
"4909","Narrated Abu Khalifa from Abu al-Walid from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd from Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: Abu Bakr sent for me at the time of the slaughter of the people of Yamama, and Umar was sitting with him. Abu Bakr said: Umar came to me and said: Slaughter has raged among the reciters of the Quran at Yamama. He said: I said: And how can I do something which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? Umar said: By Allah, it is good. He kept returning to me about that until Allah expanded my chest for what He had expanded the chest of Umar for, and I saw in that what Umar saw. Then Abu Bakr said to Zayd: You are a young, intelligent man whom we do not suspect; you used to write the revelation for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so pursue the Quran and collect it. Zayd said: By Allah, had they charged me with moving a mountain from the mountains, it would not have been heavier than what he commanded me of collecting the Quran. He said: I said: And how can you do something which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? He said: By Allah, it is good. Abu Bakr kept returning to me until Allah expanded my chest for what He had expanded the chest of Abu Bakr for. He said: So I pursued the Quran, collecting it from palm-leaf stalks, palm branches, and the chests of men, until I found the end of Surat al-Tawba with Khuzayma - or Abu Khuzayma - al-Ansari; I did not find it with anyone besides him: There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves - until the end of Baraa. And the sheets were with Abu Bakr until Allah took him, then with Umar during his life until Allah took him, then with Hafsa bint Umar."
"4910","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Ja'far ibn Awn from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi' al-Ansari from al-Zuhri from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I heard a verse from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought it but did not find it until I found it with a man from the Ansar: There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves - the verse."
"4911","Awf ibn Mujalid from Zayd ibn Thabit. Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to me, who said: narrated Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad: my father narrated to me that Awf ibn Mujalid al-Hadrami informed him - and he was a truthful man. He said: And he informed me while we were with Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, saying: I said to Zayd ibn Thabit: O Abu Sa'id, we find in Surat al-Furqan: And those who do not invoke another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery - up to His saying: And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful; and we find in Surat al-Nisa: Whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein, and Allah is angry with him and has cursed him and prepared for him a great punishment. So we find for him in one of them repentance and in the other a binding decree. Zayd ibn Thabit said: This severe one is after this lenient one by six months, so the severe one abrogated the lenient one."
"4912","Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti from Wahb ibn Baqiyya from Khalid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from Abu al-Zinad from Mujalid ibn Awf from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The verse of strictness concerning killing a soul in Surat al-Nisa was sent down six months after the one in al-Furqan, His saying: And whoever does that shall meet punishment."
"4913","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki from al-Qa'nabi from Ibn Abi Dhi'b from Uqba ibn Abd al-Rahman from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban from Zayd ibn Thabit from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"4914","Ikrima, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Umar ibn Ali from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah from Ikrima from Zayd ibn Thabit that Ali consummated marriage with Fatima (may Allah be pleased with them both) before assigning her anything."
"4915","Abu Salih al-Samman from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir al-Misri from Harmala from Ibn Wahb from Uthman ibn al-Hakam al-Judhami from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with an oath along with a witness."
"4916","Shurahbil ibn Sa'd Abu Sa'd from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil and Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi, who said: narrated Ali ibn al-Ja'd from Ibn Abi Dhi'b from Shurahbil, who said: I was in the markets with Zayd ibn Thabit, and they seized a bird, then Zayd entered and they thrust it into my hand. So he took the bird and released it, then struck the back of my neck and said: May you lose your mother, did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared inviolable what is between its two lava tracts."
"4917","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba (H). And narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba - both said: narrated Abu Usama from al-Walid ibn Kathir from Shurahbil Abu Sa'd that he entered the markets and hunted there a nuhas - meaning a bird - so Zayd ibn Thabit said: Free it, may you lose your mother; did you not know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared inviolable the hunting of birds between its two lava tracts."
"4918","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib from Shurayh ibn al-Nu'man (H). And narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti from Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh - both said: narrated Ibn Abi al-Zinad from Shurahbil ibn Sa'd that Zayd ibn Thabit found him having hunted a bird called nuhas. He said: So he took it from me, released it, and struck me, and said: O enemy of Allah, did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared inviolable what is between the two lava tracts of Medina; meaning what is between its two rocky tracts."
"4919","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Salm al-Razi from Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani from Sufyan from Ziyad ibn Sa'd from Shurahbil ibn Sa'd from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared inviolable its game; meaning Medina."
"4920","Al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh from Yahya ibn Bukayr from Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman from Amr ibn Abi Amr from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril (peace be upon him) kept enjoining me regarding the neighbour until I thought he would have him inherit."
"4921","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba (H). And narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba - both said: narrated Waki' from Kathir ibn Zayd from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab from Zayd ibn Thabit that he was asked about recitation in Zuhr and Asr, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to prolong the recitation and move his lips."
"4922","Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi (H). And narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Asfahani from Muhammad ibn al-Munakhal al-Naysaburi - both said: narrated Ibn Abi Fudayk from Ibn Mawhab from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not dispute about the Quran, for disputing about it is disbelief."
"4923","Muhammad ibn Ikrima ibn Abd al-Rahman from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd from Muhammad ibn Ikrima ibn Abd al-Rahman from Zayd ibn Thabit that he said: May Allah have mercy on Rafi' ibn Khadij - and woe - two men came disputing abusively about farmlands, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If this is your situation, then do not lease them."
"4924","Al-Muthanna Abu Jubayr from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nu'aym from Abd al-Salam ibn Harb from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwa from Jubayr ibn al-Muthanna from his father, who said: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan sent to Zayd ibn Thabit and asked him: How does he eat and drink? He said: I drink until, when my breath is cut off, I lift the vessel from my mouth; and when I eat I lick my fingers, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies."
"4925","Al-Qasim ibn Hassan from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi' ibn Umayla al-Fazari from al-Qasim ibn Hassan from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I asked him about the fear prayer. He said: The Messenger of Allah stood and prayed with them; one rank stood behind him and one rank faced the enemy, so he prayed with them one rak'a, then these went to the position of those, and those came, and he prayed with them one rak'a, then he left."
"4926","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Yahya al-Himmani and Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Tha'labi, who said: narrated Sharik from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi' from al-Qasim ibn Hassan from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us the fear prayer once; he did not pray with us before it nor after it."
"4927","Narrated Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi from al-Haytham ibn Jamil (H). And narrated Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari from Isma ibn Sulayman al-Khazzaz (H). And narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani - all said: narrated Sharik from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi' from al-Qasim ibn Hassan from Zayd ibn Thabit from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I have left among you two successors: the Book of Allah and my household; and they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond."
"4928","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Sharik from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi' from al-Qasim ibn Hassan from Zayd ibn Thabit, raising it (to the Prophet), who said: I have left among you the two successors: the Book of Allah and my progeny; and they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond."
"4929","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Umar ibn Sa'd Abu Dawud al-Hafari from Sharik from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi' from al-Qasim ibn Hassan from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am leaving among you the two weighty things after me: the Book of Allah (Mighty and Majestic) and my progeny, my household; and they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond."
"4930","Abbad ibn Shayban Abu Yahya al-Makhzumi from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from my father and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr, who said: narrated Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym from Yahya ibn Abbad from his father from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on a man who hears my saying and conveys it; for many a carrier of understanding is not understanding, and many a carrier of understanding conveys to one more understanding than him."
"4931","Wahb Abu Muhammad from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari from Abu al-Ashath Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam from Maymun ibn Zayd from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym from Muhammad ibn Wahb from his father from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah brighten a servant who hears my saying and conveys it to another, for many a carrier of understanding conveys it to one more understanding than him, and many a carrier of understanding who is not understanding. Three things over which the heart of a Muslim does not harbor deceit: sincerity of deed for Allah, sincere counsel to the rulers, and adherence to the community, for their supplication encompasses those behind them. Whoever makes this world his concern, Allah removes richness from his heart and places his poverty before his eyes, and Allah scatters his affairs, and nothing of this world comes to him except what was apportioned for him. Whoever makes the Hereafter his concern, Allah places richness in his heart, removes his poverty from before his eyes, gathers his affairs for him, and this world comes to him humbled."
"4932","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl al-Askari and Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Asbahani, who said: Narrated Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn from Muhammad ibn Jabir from Abu Farwa from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I used to write for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I had just placed the pen on my ear when fighting was commanded, when a blind man came and said: What about me, when my sight is gone? Then it was revealed: There is no blame upon the blind."
"4933","Thabit ibn Ubayd from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Yahya ibn Isa from al-Amash from Thabit ibn Ubayd from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Letters from people come to me, and I do not like everyone to read them, so can you learn the writing of Syriac? I said: Yes. So I learned it in seventeen days."
"4934","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi from Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Jarir and Yahya ibn Isa from al-Amash from Thabit ibn Ubayd from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Letters from people come to me which I do not like everyone to read, so can you learn the writing of Syriac? I said: Yes. He said: So I learned it in seventeen days."
"4935","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi from Abu Muawiya Muhammad ibn Khazim from al-Amash from Thabit ibn Ubayd from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Letters come to me, then he mentioned the like of it."
"4936","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Thalabi; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani, who said: Narrated Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash from al-Amash from Adi ibn Thabit from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Matters come to me which I dislike to be read, can you learn Syriac? I said: Yes. So I learned it in seventeen days. Abu al-Qasim said: Thus Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated it from Adi ibn Thabit, differing from the companions of al-Amash in the isnad; if he preserved it, it is strange among the hadith of Adi ibn Thabit, otherwise the hadith is as the people narrated it from al-Amash from Thabit ibn Ubayd."
"4937","Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Asbahani from Abu Yusuf al-Qulusi from Abd Allah ibn Ghalib al-Abbadani from Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahman from Mabad ibn Khalid al-Khuzai from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Every weak one deemed weak, if he swore by Allah He would fulfill it. Shall I not inform you of the people of the Fire? He said: Every harsh coarse one."
"4938","Damra ibn Habib from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Abd Allah ibn Salih; narrated to me Muawiya ibn Salih from Damra ibn Habib from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him and commanded him to enjoin upon his family with it every morning: At Your service, O Allah, at Your service, and gladly at Your obedience, and all good is in Your Hands and from You and by You and to You. O Allah, whatever word I spoke, or vow I vowed, or oath I swore, Your will precedes it; what You will is, and what You do not will is not. There is no power nor strength except by Allah, and Allah is over all things Powerful. O Allah, whatever prayer I prayed, it is upon whom You prayed, and whatever curse I invoked, it is upon whom You cursed. You are my Guardian in this world and the Hereafter; cause me to die as a Muslim and join me with the righteous. O Allah, I ask You for contentment with the decree, and coolness of life after death, and the delight of looking at Your Face, and longing to meet You, without harmful adversity nor misleading trial. I seek refuge in You from wronging or being wronged, or transgressing or being transgressed against, or acquiring a sin in error, or committing a sin. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Possessor of majesty and honor, I covenant to You in this worldly life and call You to witness, and sufficient are You as witness: I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, without partner, to You belongs dominion and to You belongs praise, and You are over all things Powerful. And I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger, and I bear witness that Your promise is true and meeting You is true and the Hour is coming without doubt, and that You will resurrect those in the graves. And I bear witness that if You leave me to myself, You leave me to weakness and exposure and sin and error, for I trust in nothing but Your mercy, so forgive me my sin, for none forgives sin but You, and turn to me in mercy, for You are the Oft-Returning, the Merciful."
"4939","Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasa al-Mahri from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasa, who informed him from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: While we were around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) compiling the Quran from scraps, he said: Glad tidings for al-Sham. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, why is that? He said: The angels of the Most Merciful spread their wings over them."
"4940","Narrated Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj from Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from Ibn Lahia from Yazid ibn Abi Habib that he heard Ibn Shimasa informing from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) writing the revelation, and he said: Glad tidings for al-Sham, three times. We said: What is that, O Prophet of Allah? He said: The angels spread their wings over al-Sham."
"4941","Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri from Harmala ibn Yahya from Ibn Wahb; informed me Amr ibn al-Harith from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Ibn Shimasa that he heard Zayd ibn Thabit saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while we were with him: Glad tidings for al-Sham. We said: What is with it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Most Merciful stretches His mercy over it."
"4942","Abu Nadra al-Mundhir ibn Malik al-Abdi from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman from al-Rabi ibn Badr from al-Jurayri from Abu Nadra from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-four to twenty-five shares."
"4943","Humayd ibn Hilal al-Adawi from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ali ibn Bahr from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra; and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman, who said: Narrated Muhammad ibn Bishr, who said: Narrated Hajjaj al-Sawwaf from Humayd ibn Hilal from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks a claim from his brother without proof, the one from whom it is sought is more entitled to the oath. And the wording is that of Ali ibn Bahr."
"4944","Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj al-Jazari from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, who said: Narrated Umar ibn Ayyub al-Mawsili from Jafar ibn Burqan from Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mukhabara. I said: What is mukhabara? He said: That you take land for a half or a third or a quarter."
"4945","Badr ibn Khalid from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Wasawisi from Damra ibn Rabia from Rabia from Abd Allah ibn Shawdhab from Abu al-Juwayriya from Badr ibn Khalid, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit stood over us on the day of the house and said: Are you not ashamed before one before whom the angels are ashamed? We said: What is that? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Uthman passed by me while with me was an angel from the angels, and he said: A martyr killed by his people, we are indeed ashamed before him. Badr said: So a group of people turned away from him."
"4946","Abd Allah ibn al-Daylami from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi from Abu Sinan from Wahb ibn Khalid al-Himyari from Ibn al-Daylami, who said: I met Zayd ibn Thabit and asked him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If Allah punished the people of His heavens and His earth, He would punish them while not wronging them, and if He had mercy on them, His mercy would be better for them than their deeds. If you had Mount Uhud and the like of Uhud in gold which you spent in the path of Allah, Allah would not accept it from you until you believe in the decree in full, and know that what befell you could never have missed you, and what missed you could never have befallen you, and that if you died upon other than this you would enter the Fire."
"4947","Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Tawus informed him that Hujr al-Madari informed him that he heard Zayd ibn Thabit saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The umra is for the heir."
"4948","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit, like the hadith of Ibn Jurayj from Amr."
"4949","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Tawus saying: Hujr al-Madari narrated to me from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning the umra that it belongs to the one given it for his life and his death."
"4950","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari from Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli, who said: We read to Maqil ibn Ubayd Allah from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants something as an umra, it belongs to the one given it for his life and his death; do not grant things as ruqba, for whoever is granted something as ruqba, it takes its course."
"4951","Narrated Abu Khalifa from Abu al-Walid from Sufyan ibn Uyayna from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned the umra to the heir."
"4952","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, who said: Narrated Hudba ibn Khalid from Hammad ibn al-Jad, who said: Qatada was asked while I was present about the umra, and he said: Narrated Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning the umra that it is valid."
"4953","Narrated Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Salih al-Marwazi al-Misri from Said ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Samman from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi from Ayyub from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The umra is valid."
"4954","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi; narrated to me Shibl ibn Abbad from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants an umra, it is his for his life and his death; do not grant things as ruqba, for whoever is granted something as ruqba, it takes the course of inheritance."
"4955","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father from Ibrahim ibn Khalid from Rabah ibn Zayd from Amr ibn Habib from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not grant ruqba; whoever is granted something as ruqba, its course is that of inheritance."
"4956","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal from Yazid ibn Zuray from Rawh ibn al-Qasim from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The umra, its course is the course of inheritance."
"4957","Narrated Muhammad ibn Musa al-Missisi from Muhammad ibn Qudama al-Jawhari from Abu Ubayda al-Haddad from Salim ibn Hayyan from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The umra and the ruqba, their course is the course of inheritance."
"4958","Narrated Ali ibn Said al-Razi from Muhammad ibn Uqba ibn Alqama al-Bayruti; narrated to me my father from al-Awzai from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The umra, its course is the course of inheritance."
"4959","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani from Abu Kurayb from Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman from Qays ibn al-Rabi from Abu Bakr, that is Wail ibn Dawud, from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The umra is inheritance."
"4960","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani from Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi; and narrated Mahmud ibn Ali al-Asbahani from Yunus ibn Habib, who said: Narrated Abu Dawud from Shuba from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The umra belongs to the heir, or he said: Its course is the course of inheritance."
"4961","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal; and narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib from Ali ibn al-Jad, who said: Narrated Hammad ibn Salama from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari that Zayd ibn Thabit said: The umra is valid."
"4962","Narrated Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi from Sulayman ibn Harb from Hammad ibn Zayd from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Hujr al-Madari from Zayd ibn Thabit that he was asked about the umra and said: Its course is the course of inheritance. Abu al-Qasim said: The two Hammads stopped it as mawquf."
"4963","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri; and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym from Sufyan from Ibn Abi Najih from Tawus from a man from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned the ruqba to the one to whom it was granted as ruqba, and the umra to the one to whom it was granted as umra."
"4964","Zayd ibn al-Harith al-Ansari, a Badri. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani; narrated to me my father from Ibn Lahia from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr among the Ansar, then of Banu Jusham ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Zayd ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj."
"4965","Zayd ibn al-Mirs al-Ansari, a Badri. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani; narrated to me my father from Ibn Lahia from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr among the Ansar, then of Banu Jazra ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, who are Banu al-Hubli: Zayd ibn al-Mirs."
"4966","Zayd ibn Wadia al-Ansari, a Badri. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Ibn Lahia from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr among the Ansar, then of Banu Salim ibn Ghanim ibn Awf ibn al-Khazraj, who are Banu al-Hubli: Zayd ibn Wadia ibn Amr ibn Qays ibn Jaz ibn Adi ibn Malik ibn Salim ibn Ghanim ibn Awf ibn al-Khazraj."
"4967","Zayd ibn Arqam al-Ansari, kunya Abu Amir, also said Abu Unaysa, also said Abu Sad. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ali ibn al-Mundhir from Muhammad ibn Fudayl from al-Amash from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Yahya ibn Jada, who said: I said to Zayd ibn Arqam: O Abu Amir."
"4968","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Junayd at al-Raqqa from Abu Salama al-Khuzai from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd ibn Jariya al-Ansari from Amr ibn Zayd ibn Haritha; narrated to me my father Zayd ibn Haritha that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) deemed young those people on the day of Uhud, among them Zayd ibn Arqam."
"4969","Ibn Abbas from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Jurayj; informed me al-Hasan ibn Muslim from Tawus, who said: Zayd ibn Arqam came, and Ibn Abbas would ask him to recall: How did you inform me about meat gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as unlawful? He said: Yes, a limb of game meat was gifted to him and he returned it to him and said: We do not eat it, for we are in ihram."
"4970","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abu Asim from Ibn Jurayj from al-Hasan ibn Muslim from Tawus from Ibn Abbas, who said: Zayd ibn Arqam came, and Ibn Abbas asked him about game meat gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram, and he returned it and said: We are in ihram."
"4971","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal; and narrated Abu Khalifa from Abu al-Walid, who said: Narrated Hammad ibn Salama from Qays ibn Sad from Ata from Ibn Abbas, who said: I said to Zayd ibn Arqam: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was gifted a limb of game while in ihram and returned it? He said: Yes, Hajjaj said: So he did not accept it, and said: We are in ihram. He said: Yes."
"4972","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Khalid ibn Makhlad from Zuhayr ibn Muawiya from Abu al-Zubayr from Tawus from Ibn Abbas from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: A leg of a donkey was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Convey greeting to him and say: Had we not been in ihram we would not have returned it."
"4973","Muawiya from Zayd ibn Arqam, may Allah be pleased with them. Narrated Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from al-Husayn ibn Salama ibn Abi Kabsha from Abu Dawud from Shuba from Abu Abd Allah al-Shami, who said: I heard Muawiya delivering a sermon saying: O people of al-Sham, the Ansari narrated to me, Shuba said: meaning Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will always be people of my umma fighting upon the truth until the matter comes to them, and I think you are them, O people of al-Sham."
"4974","Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathila from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani from Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat from Abd al-Rahman ibn Musab from Fitr ibn Khalifa from Abu al-Tufayl from Zayd ibn Arqam that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomsoever I am his wali, Ali is his wali."
"4975","Narrated Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini; narrated Kathir ibn Yahya from Abu Kathir ibn Yahya from Abu Awana and Said ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Salit al-Hanafi from al-Amash from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Amr ibn Wathila from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the Farewell Pilgrimage and alighted at Ghadir Khumm, he ordered the large trees cleared, then he stood and said: As though I have been called and I answered; I leave among you the two weighty things, one of them greater than the other: the Book of Allah and my kin, my household. See how you succeed me concerning them, for they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond. Then he said: Allah is my Master, and I am the wali of every believer. Then he took the hand of Ali and said: Whomsoever I am his mawla, this one is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him. I said to Zayd: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: There was no one among the large trees but that he saw it with his eyes and heard it with his ears."
"4976","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani from Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani, who said: Narrated Sharik from al-Amash from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu al-Tufayl from Zayd ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"4977","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Jafar ibn Humayd; narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba; narrated al-Nadr ibn Said Abu Suhayb, who said: Narrated Abd Allah ibn Bukayr from Hakim ibn Jubayr from Abu al-Tufayl from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted on the day of al-Juhfa, then turned to the people, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: I find for a prophet only half the lifespan of the one before him, and I am about to be called and I shall answer. What will you say? They said: You counseled. He said: Do you not bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that Paradise is true and the Fire is true, and that resurrection after death is true? They said: We bear witness. He said: So he raised his hands and placed them on his chest, then said: And I bear witness with you. Then he said: Do you not hear? They said: Yes. He said: I precede you at the Pond, and you will come to me at the Pond, and its breadth is farther than between Sana and Busra; in it are cups of silver numbering the stars. See how you succeed me concerning the two weighty things? A caller called: What are the two weighty things, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Book of Allah, one end in the Hand of Allah Almighty and one end in your hands, so hold fast to it and do not go astray; and the other is my kin. The All-Subtle, the All-Aware informed me that they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond, and I asked that for them from my Lord, so do not go ahead of them lest you perish, and do not fall short of them lest you perish, and do not teach them, for they are more knowledgeable than you. Then he took the hand of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Whomsoever I am nearer to than himself, Ali is his wali. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."
"4978","Anas ibn Malik from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Masada ibn Sad al-Attar al-Makki from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami; and narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, who said: Narrated Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Zayd ibn Arqam wrote to me, having learned of my grief over those of my people struck at al-Harra, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar, and Ibn al-Fadl doubted concerning the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"4979","Qutba ibn Malik from Zayd Arqam. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal; narrated to me my father; and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, who said: Narrated Waki from Misar from Abu Ayyub, freedman of Banu Thalaba, from Qutba ibn Malik, who said: A commander among the commanders reviled Ali, so Zayd ibn Arqam stood to him and said: You indeed knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade reviling the dead, so why do you revile Ali when he has died?"
"4980","Narrated Abu al-Shaykh Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asbahani and al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Zakariya, who said: Narrated Muhammad al-Saqati from Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Razin from Shuba from Misar from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa from his uncle that al-Mughira ibn Shuba said: Who is Ali! So Zayd ibn Arqam stood to him and said: O Mughira, did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade reviling the dead? So why do you revile Ali when he has died?"
"4981","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal; narrated to me my father from Muhammad ibn Bishr; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Ibn al-Mubarak, who said: Narrated Misar from al-Hajjaj, freedman of Banu Thalaba, from Qutba ibn Malik from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, who said: A man disparaged Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, so Zayd ibn Arqam said to him: You indeed knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid reviling the dead."
"4982","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Shuba from al-Hakam from Ibn Abi Layla, who said: I prayed behind Zayd ibn Arqam over a funeral and he magnified four times over it, then I prayed behind him over another and he magnified five times over it. So I asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to magnify them."
"4983","Narrated Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi from Amr ibn Marzuq; narrated Shuba from Amr ibn Murra from Abu Hamza, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam saying: We said: O Messenger of Allah, every people has followers, and we have followed you, so supplicate Allah to make our followers of us! So he supplicated. Amr ibn Murra said: So I related that to Ibn Abi Layla, and he said: Zayd ibn Arqam claimed that."
"4984","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abu al-Walid from Shuba from Amr ibn Murra from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: When we said to Zayd ibn Arqam: Narrate to us, he said: We have grown old and forgotten, and narration from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is weighty."
"4985","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Asad ibn Musa; and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Masruq ibn al-Marzuban, who said: Narrated Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida from al-Amash from Amr ibn Murra from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: When Ibn Ubayy said what he said, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him; he came and swore he did not say it, and people began saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with lying, until I sat in the house fearing that when they saw me they would say: This is the one who lies, until Allah Almighty revealed: They are the ones who say."
"4986","Abu al-Duha Muslim ibn Subayh from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti from Khalid ibn Abd Allah from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah from Abu al-Duha from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I leave among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah and my kin, my household, and they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond."
"4987","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Ali ibn al-Madini from Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah from Abu al-Duha from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I leave among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah and my kin, my household, and they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond."
"4988","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from al-Himmani from Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah from Abu al-Duha from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"4989","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi from Ali ibn Abis from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah from Abu al-Duha from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."
"4990","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Dirar ibn Surad from Ali ibn Abis from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah from Abu al-Duha from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicate and raise his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits."
"4991","Zayd ibn Wahb from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Asbahani from Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali from Abu Israil al-Mulai from al-Hakam from Abu Sulayman Zayd ibn Wahb from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: Ali adjured the people at al-Rahba: Whoever heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying what he said to him, so sixteen men stood and bore witness that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him. Zayd ibn Arqam said: I was among those who concealed, so my sight went away, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, had supplicated against whoever concealed."
"4992","Yahya ibn Jada from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym from Kamil Abu al-Ala, who said: I heard Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrating from Yahya ibn Jada from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we ended at Ghadir Khumm; he ordered the large trees cleared in a day, no day harder in heat having come upon us. He praised Allah and extolled Him and said: O people, no prophet was ever sent but that he lived half of what the one before him lived, and I am about to be called and I shall answer, and I leave among you what you will never go astray after: the Book of Allah. Then he stood and took the hand of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: O people, who is nearer to you than yourselves? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla."
"4993","Abd Khayr al-Hadrami from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from Salih from al-Shabi from Abd Khayr al-Hadrami from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was in Yemen when a woman was brought to him with whom three men had intercourse in one purity period, so he asked two: Do you affirm this child for this one? They did not affirm. Then he asked two: Do you affirm this one for this child? Then he asked two, until he finished, then he asked two about one, and they did not affirm. So he cast lots among them, imposed the child on the one upon whom the lot fell, and placed upon him two-thirds of the blood-money. That was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he laughed until his molars appeared."
"4994","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani from Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat; narrated Abd al-Razzaq from Sufyan from al-Ajlah from al-Shabi from Abd Khayr from Zayd ibn Arqam, the like of it."
"4995","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Khalid ibn Sulayman al-Shaybani from Amir from a man of Hadramawt from Zayd ibn Arqam that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was in Yemen when three men came to him disputing over a child, each claiming he is his son. He secluded himself with two and said: Are your souls content to give the child to this one? They said: No. Then he secluded himself with two and said to them the like of that, and they said: No. He said: I see you as quarrelsome partners, and I shall cast lots among you. So he cast lots among them, gave the child to the one struck by the lot, and fined him two-thirds of the blood-money for the remaining two."
"4996","Abd Allah ibn al-Khalil from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi from Sufyan from al-Ajlah; and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Ali ibn Mushir from al-Ajlah; and narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Khalid from al-Ajlah; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Abd Allah ibn Numayr; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani; and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Jubara ibn al-Mughallis, who said: Narrated Qays ibn al-Rabi from al-Ajlah; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash from al-Ajlah from al-Shabi from Abd Allah ibn al-Khalil from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali to Yemen, and he was brought three men who had intercourse with a woman in one purity period, and she bore a child. He began saying to each one: Are you content that the child belong to this one? You are quarrelsome partners. So he cast lots among them, gave the child to the one struck by the lot, and placed upon him two-thirds of the blood-money for the other two. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he laughed until his molars appeared."
"4997","Ali ibn Durri al-Hadrami from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Jandal ibn Waliq from Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman; and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Jarir from Muhammad ibn Salim from Asim ibn Ali ibn Durri al-Hadrami from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a letter came to him from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, in it that three men came to me disputing over a boy whose mother they had intercourse with in the pre-Islamic time in one purity period, each claiming him as his son. So I judged among them that I cast lots among them, and gave him to the winner among them, upon fining the other two two-thirds of the blood-money. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his canines appeared, then said: I know in it nothing but what Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, judged."
"4998","Narrated Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli from Ali ibn al-Madini from Sufyan from Muhammad ibn Salim from al-Shabi from Ali ibn Dharih from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the like of it."
"4999","Narrated Abd al-Wahhab ibn Rawaha al-Ramahurmuzi from Abu Kurayb from Abd Allah ibn Ismail al-Azdi from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani from al-Shabi from a man from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali as governor over Yemen, and he was brought buried treasure, so he took a fifth from it and gave the rest to its owner. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it pleased him."
"5000","Abu Salman al-Muadhdhin from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym from al-Ala ibn Salih; narrated Abu Salman that he prayed with Zayd ibn Arqam over a funeral and he magnified five takbirs over it. I said: Did you err or deliberately? He said: Rather deliberately; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray it so."
"5001","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi; and narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Said ibn Sulayman, who said: Narrated Sharik from Uthman ibn Abi Zura from Abu Salman al-Muadhdhin, who said: Abu Sariha al-Ghifari died, and Zayd ibn Arqam prayed over him and magnified four times over him, and said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying."
"5002","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Abu Israil al-Mulai from al-Hakam from Abu Salman al-Muadhdhin from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: Ali adjured the people: I adjure by Allah a man who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him. So twelve Badri men stood and bore witness to that. Zayd said: And I was among those who concealed, so my sight went away."
"5003","Talha ibn Yazid Abu Hamza, freedman of Qaraza, al-Ansari from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abu al-Walid and Sulayman ibn Harb; and narrated Abu Khalifa from Abu Umar al-Hawdi from Shuba from Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Abu Hamza saying: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You are one part of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond. I said: How many were you that day? He said: Seven hundred men or eight hundred men."
"5004","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from his father; and narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from his father; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, who said: Narrated Jarir from al-Amash from Amr ibn Murra from Talha ibn Yazid al-Ansari, who said: Zayd ibn Arqam said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are one part of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond. I said: How many were you that day? He said: Six hundred or seven hundred."
"5005","Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti from Abu al-Shatha from Hafs ibn Ghiyath from al-Amash from Amr ibn Murra from Talha, freedman of Qaraza, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey in a campaign, and he said: You are but one part of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond on the Day of Resurrection. They said to Zayd: How many were you that day? He said: Between eight hundred and seven hundred."
"5006","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Abu Muawiya; and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ibrahim ibn Abi Muawiya; narrated to me my father; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Abu Muawiya from al-Amash from Amr ibn Murra from Talha ibn Yazid from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: You are but one part of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond. We said to Zayd: How many were you that day? He said: Between six hundred and seven hundred."
"5007","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Waki from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Murra from his father from Talha ibn Yazid from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Today you are but one part of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond. I said: How many were you that day? He said: Seven hundred or eight hundred."
"5008","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abu al-Walid from Shuba from Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Abu Hamza saying: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam saying: The first to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Ali. So I narrated that to Ibrahim, and he denied that and said: The first to pray was Abu Bakr."
"5009","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh from his father from Shuba from Amr ibn Murra from Abu Hamza from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul saying: Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and Ibn Ubayy came to him and swore to him that he did not say that, and the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and blamed me. So I came to my dwelling and slept, as though grieved. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me, so I came to him, or he said: So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Allah has confirmed you and excused you, and recited these two verses: They are the ones who say: Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah, until he sealed the two verses."
"5010","Thumama ibn Uqba al-Muhallimi from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Minjab ibn al-Harith from Ali ibn Mushir from al-Amash from Thumama ibn Uqba from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: A man of the People of the Book came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu al-Qasim, you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink, yet one who eats and drinks needs to relieve himself! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The need of one of them is sweat pouring from his skin, whereupon his belly shrinks."
"5011","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father from Yala ibn Ubayd from al-Amash from Thumama ibn Uqba from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: You claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink! He said: Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, a man among them is given the strength of a hundred men in eating and drinking and intercourse and desire. He said: One who eats and drinks needs to relieve himself! He said: Sweat, and when that is so his belly shrinks."
"5012","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Waki from al-Amash from Thumama ibn Uqba al-Muhallimi from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of the people of Paradise is given the strength of a hundred men in eating and drinking and desire and intercourse. A man of the Jews said: One who eats and drinks needs to relieve himself! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The need of one of them is sweat pouring from his skin, whereupon his belly shrinks."
"5013","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Abu Muawiya from al-Amash from Thumama ibn Uqba from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5014","Narrated Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai; narrated Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi from Musab ibn al-Miqdam from Dawud al-Tai from al-Amash from Thumama ibn Uqba from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: A man of the People of the Book said: O Abu al-Qasim, you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, one of them is given the strength of a hundred men in eating and drinking and intercourse and desire. He said: One who eats needs to relieve himself! He said: The need of one of them is sweat like the scent of musk, whereupon his belly shrinks."
"5015","Narrated Ali ibn Bishr al-Maqaridi al-Sanani from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Huti al-Sanani from Said ibn Salim from Ali ibn Salih al-Makki from al-Amash from Thumama ibn Uqba al-Muhallimi from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: A man of the People of the Book came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu al-Qasim, you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, a man is given the strength of a hundred men in eating and drinking and intercourse and desire."
"5016","Narrated Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti from Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan from Yahya ibn Rashid from Abd al-Nur ibn Abd Allah ibn Sinan from Harun ibn Sad from Thumama ibn Uqba, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam saying: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man of the Jews said to him: Do you claim that in Paradise there is food and drink and spouses? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. The Jew said: We find it good, made good! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you believe in the tree of musk and find it in your book? He said: Yes. He said: Urine and major impurity are sweat flowing from their forelocks to their feet like musk."
"5017","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from his father; and narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from his father; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba; and narrated Abu Khalifa from Ali ibn al-Madini, who said: Narrated Jarir from al-Amash from Thumama ibn Uqba from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: A man used to visit the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he tied knots for him and placed them in the well of a man of the Ansar. Two angels came to him visiting him; one sat at his head and the other at his feet. One said: Do you know what ails him? He said: So-and-so who visits him tied knots for him and cast them into the well of so-and-so the Ansari. If a man were sent to take the knots, he would find the water turned yellow. He said: So he sent a man who took the knots and untied them, and he recovered. Thereafter the man would visit the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), yet he did not mention anything of it to him nor reproach him for it, upon him be peace."
"5018","Narrated Abu Khalifa from Ali ibn al-Madini from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa from Shayban from al-Amash from Thumama ibn Uqba from Zayd ibn Arqam, as Jarir said."
"5019","Narrated Abu Khalifa from Ali ibn al-Madini from Abu Muawiya from al-Amash from Yazid ibn Hayyan from Zayd ibn Arqam, similar, though Jarir differed from Shayban in its isnad."
"5020","Narrated Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti from Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan from Yahya ibn Rashid from Abd al-Nur ibn Abd Allah from Harun ibn Sad from Thumama ibn Uqba from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: While I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man of the Jews called Thalaba ibn al-Harith came and said: Peace upon you, O Muhammad. He said: And upon you."
"5021","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani and Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti, who said: Narrated Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi from Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar from Shuba from Harun ibn Sad from Thumama ibn Uqba from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) greeted us concluding the prayer, we said: And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings."
"5022","Yazid ibn Hayyan al-Taymi from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Abu Muawiya from al-Amash from Yazid ibn Hayyan from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: A man of the Jews bewitched the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he complained of that for days. Jibril, upon him be peace, came to him and said: A man of the Jews bewitched you, tying knots for you! The Messenger of Allah sent Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, to him, and he extracted them and brought them. Each time he untied a knot he found relief from that, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as though freed from fetters. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) neither mentioned that Jew nor ever saw him in his face."
"5023","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Ibn al-Asbahani from Amr ibn Thabit from Yazid ibn Hayyan from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"5024","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal; narrated to me my father from Ismail ibn Ibrahim from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi; narrated to me Yazid ibn Hayyan al-Taymi, who said: I went with Husayn ibn Sabra and Amr ibn Muslim to Zayd ibn Arqam, and he said: My ears heard and my heart retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"5025","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, who said: Narrated Musaddad from Yahya ibn Said from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi from Yazid ibn Hayyan from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: My ears heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"5026","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Yala ibn Ubayd from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi from Yazid ibn Hayyan from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"5027","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Jarir from Abu Hayyan from Yazid ibn Hayyan from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad sent for me, so I came to him. He said: What reports reach us from you which you narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that we do not find in the Book of Allah? You narrate that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has a Pond? He said: I said: He narrated that to us and promised it to us. He said: You lie, but you are an old man who has doted. He said: I said: My ears indeed heard and my heart retained him saying: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell, so I did not lie upon him."
"5028","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yahya from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi; narrated to me Yazid ibn Hayyan al-Taymi from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad sent for me: What reports reach us from you which you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), claiming he has a Pond in Paradise? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated that to us and promised it to us. He said: You lie, but you are an old man who has doted."
"5029","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from Yazid ibn Hayyan al-Taymi, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam, and it was said to him: Who are the family of Muhammad? He said: Those upon whom charity is unlawful? It was said: Who are they? He said: The family of Ali, and the family of Aqil, and the family of Jafar, and the family of al-Abbas."
"5030","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Fudayl ibn Abd al-Wahhab from Sharik from al-Amash from Yazid ibn Hayyan, who said: I asked Zayd ibn Arqam: Who are the family of Muhammad? He said: They are the family of Ali, and the family of al-Abbas, and the family of Jafar, and the family of Aqil."
"5031","Narrated Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini from Kathir ibn Yahya from Abu Awana from al-Amash from Yazid ibn Hayyan from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I leave among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah and my kin. See how you succeed me concerning them. We said: Who are his household? He said: The family of Ali, and the family of Jafar, and the family of Aqil, and the family of al-Abbas."
"5032","Narrated Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini from Kathir ibn Yahya from Hayyan ibn Ibrahim from Said ibn Masruq, or Sufyan al-Thawri, from Yazid ibn Hayyan from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We visited him and said: You have seen good; you accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prayed behind him. He said: You have seen good, and I fear I was only delayed for evil. Whatever he narrates to you, accept it, and whatever he is silent about, leave it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in a valley between Mecca and Medina and addressed us, then said: I am a man about to be called and I shall answer, and I leave among you two, one of them the Book of Allah in which is the rope of Allah; whoever follows it is upon guidance, and whoever leaves it is upon misguidance. And my household; I remind you of Allah concerning my household, three times. We said: Who are his household? His wives? He said: No; a woman a man may marry for a time, then divorce her, and she returns to her father and mother. His household are his family and his kin who were forbidden charity after him: the family of Ali, and the family of al-Abbas, and the family of Jafar, and the family of Aqil."
"5033","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Waki from his father from Said ibn Masruq from Yazid ibn Hayyan from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I adjure you by Allah concerning my household. We said to Zayd: Who are his household? He said: Those forbidden charity: the family of Ali, and the family of al-Abbas, and the family of Aqil, and the family of Jafar."
"5034","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani, who said: Narrated Muhammad ibn Fudayl; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Ismail ibn Ibrahim, all from Abu Hayyan from Yazid ibn Hayyan, who said: I went with Husayn ibn Sabra and Umar ibn Muslim to Zayd ibn Arqam. When we sat with him, Husayn ibn Sabra said to him: O Zayd, you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard his hadith and campaigned with him; you have attained much good, O Zayd. Narrate to us, O Zayd, what you witnessed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and what you heard! He said: O son of my brother, by Allah my age has grown and my time is distant, and I forgot some of what I retained of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Whatever I narrate to you, accept it, and whatever I do not narrate to you, do not burden me with it. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood one day among us as preacher at a water called Khumm between Mecca and Medina. He praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him and exhorted and reminded, then said: To proceed, O people, I am but a man about to have the messenger of my Lord come to me and I shall answer him, and I leave among you the two weighty things, one of them the Book of Allah in which is guidance and light. Take the Book of Allah and hold fast to it. So he urged upon the Book of Allah and inclined toward it, then said: My household; I remind you of Allah concerning my household. He said it three times. Husayn said to him: Who are his household, O Zayd? Are not his wives of his household? He said: His wives are of his household, but his household are those forbidden charity after him. He said: Who are they? He said: They are the family of Ali, and the family of Jafar, and the family of al-Abbas, and the family of Aqil. It was said: Were all these forbidden charity? He said: Yes."
"5035","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Yahya al-Himmani from Qays ibn al-Rabi from Yazid ibn Hayyan, who said: I asked Zayd ibn Arqam: Who are the family of Muhammad? He said: The family of Ali, and the family of al-Abbas, and the family of Aqil, and the family of Jafar."
"5036","Subayh, freedman of Umm Salama, from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, who said: Narrated Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail from Asbat ibn Nasr al-Hamdani from al-Suddi from Subayh, freedman of Umm Salama, from Zayd ibn Arqam that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali and Fatima and Hasan and Husayn: I am at peace with whoever is at peace with you, and at war with whoever wars against you."
"5037","Narrated Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani from Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari from Husayn ibn Muhammad from Sulayman ibn Qarm from Abu al-Jahhaf from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Subayh from his grandfather from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a house in which were Fatima and Ali and Hasan and Husayn, and said: I am at war with whoever wars against them, and at peace with whoever is at peace with them."
"5038","Habib ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym from Yusuf ibn Suhayb; narrated Habib ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We used to recite in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold or silver he would wish for a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever turns."
"5039","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym from Yusuf ibn Suhayb from Habib ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not trim his mustache is not of us."
"5040","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Mindal ibn Ali from Yusuf ibn Suhayb from Habib ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not trim his mustache is not of us."
"5041","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Durays from Musab ibn Sallam from al-Zibriqan al-Sarraj from Habib ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not trim his mustache is not of us."
"5042","Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi from Jamil ibn Yazid al-Marwazi from al-Musayyab ibn Sharik from Hamza al-Zayyat from Yusuf ibn Suhayb from Habib ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not trim his mustache."
"5043","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Usayd al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Bazigh al-Jazzar from Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Asyaghi from Yusuf ibn Suhayb from Habib ibn Yasar, who said: When al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was struck, Zayd ibn Arqam stood at the door of the mosque and said: Did you do it? I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, I entrust them two and the righteous believers to You. It was said to Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad: Zayd ibn Arqam said such-and-such. He said: That is an old man whose mind has gone."
"5044","Abu al-Minhal from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Affan from Shuba from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, who said: I heard Abu al-Minhal saying: I asked al-Bara ibn Azib and Zayd ibn Arqam about exchange, and this one says: Ask this one, and this one says: Ask this one, for he is better than me and more knowledgeable. Both said that. So I asked them both and they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling silver for gold on credit."
"5045","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yahya from Shuba; narrated Amr ibn Dinar from Abu al-Minhal from al-Bara and Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while we were exchanging, and said: There is no harm in it hand to hand, but deferred payment is disliked."
"5046","Ali ibn Rabia al-Walibi from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail from Israil from Uthman ibn al-Mughira from Ali ibn Rabia, who said: I met Zayd ibn Arqam entering to al-Mukhtar or leaving, he said: I said a hadith that reached me from you: You heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I leave among you the two weighty things, the Book of Allah and my kin? He said: Yes."
"5047","Abu Sad al-Azdi from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba; and narrated Abu Khalifa from Ali ibn al-Madini, who said: Narrated Ubayd Allah ibn Musa from Israil from al-Suddi from Abu Sad al-Azdi; narrated Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with us were people of the Bedouins who would precede us. The Bedouin would precede his companions, filling the trough and placing stones around it, and placing the leather mat over it until his companions came. A man of the Ansar came to a Bedouin and loosened the halter of his she-camel to drink, but he refused to let him. So he pulled a stone and the water drained away, and with the Bedouin was a stick with which he struck the head of the Ansari and wounded him. He came to Abd Allah ibn Ubayy, head of the hypocrites, and informed him, and he was of his companions. Abd Allah ibn Ubayy grew angry, then said: Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse from around him, meaning the Bedouins, and they would attend the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at food. Abd Allah said to his companions: When they disperse from Muhammad, bring Muhammad food so he and those with him eat. Then he said to his companions: When you return to Medina, let the mightier of you expel the humbler. Zayd said: And I was riding behind my uncle, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: So I heard Abd Allah ibn Ubayy, and we were his maternal nephews, so I informed my uncle, who went and informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for him, and he swore and denied. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) believed him and disbelieved me. My uncle came and said: You intended nothing but that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hate you and the Muslims belie you! There befell me of grief what never befell anyone. While I was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, my head nodding from grief, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rubbed my ear and laughed in my face. Nothing would have pleased me in exchange for it like eternity in this world. Then Abu Bakr caught up with me and said: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to you? I said: He said nothing to me except that he rubbed my ear and laughed in my face. He said: Rejoice! Then Umar caught up with me, and I said to him like my saying to Abu Bakr. When morning came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Surat al-Munafiqun."
"5048","Abu Ishaq al-Sabii from Zayd. Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Sulayman ibn Harb; and narrated Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi from Abu al-Walid; and narrated Abu Khalifa from Abu al-Walid and Muhammad ibn Kathir, who said: Narrated Shuba from Abu Ishaq, who said: People went out seeking rain, and among them went out Zayd ibn Arqam. I drew near to him and said: How many campaigns did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) undertake? He said: Nineteen campaigns. I said: How many did you campaign with him? He said: Seventeen campaigns. He said: And he prayed with the people two rakas. Abu al-Walid added in his hadith: I said: What was the first the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) campaigned? He said: Dhu al-Ushayra or Dhu al-Usayra."
"5049","Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani; narrated to me my father from Zuhayr from Abu Ishaq; narrated to me Zayd ibn Arqam that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) campaigned nineteen times."
"5050","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani, who said: Narrated Khallad ibn Yazid al-Arqat al-Bahili from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq from Abu Ishaq from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seventeen campaigns."
"5051","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Asbahani al-Khuzai from Sahl ibn Muhammad al-Askari; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani, who said: Narrated Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash from Abu Ishaq from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seventeen campaigns, and two escaped me."
"5052","Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti; narrated Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi from Israil from Abu Ishaq from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seventeen campaigns. I said: How many did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) campaign? He said: Nineteen campaigns."
"5053","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr from Waki from Israil from Abu Ishaq from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seventeen campaigns; he preceded me by two campaigns."
"5054","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr from Waki from his father from Abu Ishaq from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seventeen campaigns; he preceded me by two campaigns."
"5055","Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani; narrated to me my father from Zuhayr from Abu Ishaq; narrated to me Zayd ibn Arqam that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed after emigrating one pilgrimage and did not perform after it: the Farewell Pilgrimage."
"5056","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani; narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani; narrated to me my father, who said: Narrated Zuhayr from Abu Ishaq that he heard Zayd ibn Arqam saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey in which people suffered hardship, and Abd Allah ibn Ubayy said to his companions: Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse from around him, and said: If we return to Medina, the mightier will surely expel the humbler therefrom. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He sent for Abd Allah and asked him, and he strove with his oath and said: He lied, O Messenger of Allah! There fell into my soul from what they said severity, until Allah revealed my confirmation in: When the hypocrites come to you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them to seek forgiveness for them, but they turned their heads aside, and His saying: As though they were propped timbers. He said: They were men, the most handsome of things."
"5057","Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti from Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi from Israil from Abu Ishaq from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I was with my uncle in a campaign, and I heard Abd Allah ibn Ubayy saying: Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse from around him, and: If we return to Medina, the mightier will surely expel the humbler therefrom. So I mentioned that to my uncle, who mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul and his companions, and they swore they did not say. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disbelieved me and believed him. Grief befell me like never befell me, and I sat in the house. My uncle said to me: You intended nothing but that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) belie you and hate you! So Allah Almighty revealed: When the hypocrites come to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me and recited it, then said: Allah Almighty has confirmed you."
"5058","Narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi from Salim ibn Qutayba from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam saying: My eyes inflamed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me for the inflammation and said: O Zayd, if your eyes were for what ails them, what would you do? He said: I would be patient and expectant. He said: O Zayd, if your eyes were for what ails them and you were patient and expectant, you would have no reward short of Paradise."
"5059","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Ishaq ibn Sulayman from Abu Sinan al-Shaybani from Abu Ishaq from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: When: Not equal are those of the believers who sit and those who strive in the path of Allah was revealed, Ibn Umm Maktum came and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there no concession for me? He said: No. Ibn Umm Maktum said: O Allah, I am blind, so grant me concession! So Allah revealed: Except those with disability. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered it written."
"5060","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq; narrated to me my father; narrated al-Husayn ibn Waqid from Abu Ishaq from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: People fled from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn, and he said: I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib."
"5061","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Abu Nuaym Dirar ibn Surad from Musa ibn Uthman al-Hadrami from Abu Ishaq from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"5062","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Maymun from Musa ibn Uthman al-Hadrami from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara and Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Your blood and your wealth are unlawful to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours in this land of yours."
"5063","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Dirar ibn Surad; and narrated Musa ibn Harun and Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi, who said: Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi, who said: Narrated Musa ibn Uthman al-Hadrami from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara and Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Ghadir Khumm, lifting the branch of the tree from his head, and he said: Charity is not lawful for me nor for my household. May Allah curse whoever claims to other than his father, and may Allah curse whoever allies to other than his patrons. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. There is no bequest for an heir."
"5064","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Asbahani from Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali from Amr ibn Thabit from Abu Ishaq from Hubayra ibn Yarim from Said ibn Wahb and Habba al-Urani and Zayd ibn Arqam that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, adjured the people: Whoever heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whomsoever I am his wali, Ali is his wali. A dozen or so stood and bore witness that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whomsoever I am his wali, Ali is his wali."
"5065","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Ali ibn Harb al-Jundayshaburi from Ishaq ibn Ismail Hayyawayh from Hubayb ibn Habib, brother of Hamza al-Zayyat, from Abu Ishaq from Amr ibn Dhi Murr and Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on the day of Ghadir Khumm and said: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him, and support whoever supports him, and aid whoever aids him."
"5066","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Ali ibn Harb al-Jundayshaburi from Ishaq ibn Ismail Hayyawayh from Hubayb ibn Habib, brother of Hamza al-Zayyat, from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii from Amr ibn Dhi Murr and Zayd ibn Arqam that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, shall I not teach you a supplication with which you supplicate, that if you had sins numbering the dust they would be forgiven for you, though you are forgiven? Say: O Allah, there is no god but You, the Wise, the Generous; blessed are You, glory be to You, Lord of the Mighty Throne."
"5067","Al-Shabi from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Thalaba from Abu Yahya al-Himmani from Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir from al-Shabi from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then he sent me to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then he sent me to Uthman, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise upon a trial befalling him. Uthman took my hand and went with me until he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this trial befalling me? By Allah, I neither sang nor wished, nor touched my private part with my right hand since I embraced Islam or since I pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor committed adultery in pre-Islamic time nor in Islam! He said to him: Allah will dress you in a shirt; if the hypocrites want you to take it off, do not take it off."
"5068","Abu Amr al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yahya from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid; narrated to me al-Harith ibn Shubayl from Abu Amr al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We used to speak in prayer, one of us speaking to his brother about his need, until the verse was revealed: Guard the prayers and the middle prayer, and stand for Allah devoutly. So we were commanded to be silent."
"5069","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi from his father from Marwan ibn Muawiya from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid from al-Harith ibn Shubayl from Abu Amr al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We used to, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), speak in prayer, one of us speaking to his companion about the need between him and him, until was revealed: Guard the prayers and the middle prayer, and stand for Allah devoutly. So we were then commanded to be silent."
"5070","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad from his father from Yala ibn Ubayd from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid from al-Harith ibn Shubayl from Abu Amr al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We were in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when in prayer if one of us wanted something he spoke to him and whispered to him between him and him, until this verse was revealed: And stand for Allah devoutly. So we were commanded to be silent."
"5071","Abu Abd Allah al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Asbahani from Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali from Yahya ibn Salama ibn Kuhayl from his father from Abu Abd Allah al-Shaybani, who said: I was sitting in the gathering of Banu al-Arqam when a man of Murad came riding his mount until he stopped at the gathering and greeted. He said: Is Zayd among the people? They said: Yes, this is Zayd. He said: I adjure you by Allah besides Whom there is no god, O Zayd, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Ali: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him? He said: Yes, so the man turned away from him."
"5072","Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhita from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Umari from Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Bahili from Abu al-Jawwab from Sulayman ibn Qarm from Harun ibn Sad from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhita from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of al-Ghadir and said: Am I not nearer to the believers than themselves? They said: Yes. So he took the hand of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."
"5073","Ziyad ibn Mutarrif from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Said al-Razi from Ibrahim ibn Isa al-Tanukhi from Yahya ibn Yala al-Aslami from Ammar ibn Zurayq from Abu Ishaq from Ziyad ibn Mutarrif from Zayd ibn Arqam, and sometimes he did not mention Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves to live my life and die my death and dwell in the Garden of eternity which my Lord promised me, for my Lord Almighty planted its reeds with His Hand, let him take Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, as wali, for he will never take you out of my guidance nor enter you into misguidance."
"5074","Abu Layla al-Hadrami from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani from Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat from Asim ibn Mihja from Yunus ibn Arqam from al-Amash from Abu Layla al-Hadrami from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Am I not nearer to you than yourselves? They said: Yes. He said: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla."
"5075","Atiya al-Awfi from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi from Aththam ibn Ali from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman from Atiya from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him. So I began asking him for more, and he said: I only stop where I was stopped."
"5076","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ammar ibn Khalid from Ishaq ibn al-Azraq from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman from Atiyya from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out at al-Juhfa on the day of Ghadir Khumm while holding Ali by the upper arm, and said: ""O people, do you not know that I have more authority over the believers than their own selves?"" They said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""So whomever I am his mawla, then this one is his mawla."""
"5077","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Musab ibn al-Miqdam from Fudayl ibn Marzuq from Atiyya from Zayd ibn Arqam, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whomever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla."""
"5078","Narrated Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd al-Bazzaz al-Baghdadi from Dawud ibn Rushayd from Muhammad ibn Rabia from Khalid ibn Tahman Abu al-Ala al-Khaffaf from Atiyya al-Awfi from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""How can I enjoy comfort when the bearer of the Trumpet has already seized the Trumpet, waiting for when he will be commanded to blow into it?"" They said: Then what should we say? He said: ""Say: Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best Disposer of affairs."""
"5079","Khalifa ibn Husayn from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi from Qays ibn al-Rabi, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Hasan ibn Atiyya from Qays ibn al-Rabi from al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah from Khalifa ibn Husayn from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: I was sitting with Abd Allah ibn Ubayy when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by with some of his Companions, and Abd Allah ibn Ubayy said: ""If we return to Medina, the mightier will surely expel the lowlier from it!"" So I went to Sad ibn Ubada and informed him, and he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Abd Allah ibn Ubayy, and Abd Allah ibn Ubayy swore to him by Allah that he had not said this. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked toward Sad ibn Ubada, who said: O Messenger of Allah, it was only the boy Zayd ibn Arqam who informed me of it! Then Sad came and took me by the hand and set off with me, and said: This is the one who reported to me. Abd Allah ibn Ubayy then scolded me harshly. I came to the Messenger of Allah weeping and said: Yes indeed, by the One Who sent down the light and prophethood upon you, he certainly said it! The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him, and then Allah the Almighty revealed: ""When the hypocrites come to you,"" to the end of the sura."
"5080","Nufay ibn al-Harith Abu Dawud from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from al-Haytham ibn Jammaz from Abu Dawud al-Darimi from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, sincerely, will enter Paradise."" He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""His sincerity is that it restrains him from what Allah has forbidden him."""
"5081","Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from al-Qasim ibn Sallam ibn Miskin, who related to me from his father, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Hudba ibn Khalid from Sallam ibn Miskin from Aidh Allah from Abu Dawud from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are these sacrifices? He said: ""The sunna of your father Ibrahim."" They said: Then what reward do we have in them? He said: ""For every hair, a good deed."" They said: And the wool? He said: ""For every hair, a good deed."""
"5082","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Muhammad ibn Yala Zunbur from Umar ibn al-Subh from Khalid ibn Maymun from Nufay ibn al-Harith from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not assign My servants, the knowing monotheists among the sinners, to Paradise or to Hell until I am the One Who settles them according to My knowledge of them; and do not burden yourselves with what you have not been burdened with, and do not call the servants to account apart from their Lord."""
"5083","Narrated al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi from Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti from Yazid ibn Harun from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah from Nufay or Anfa from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Allah the Almighty is with the judge so long as he does not deliberately act unjustly, guiding him to good so long as he does not intend otherwise."""
"5084","Zayd al-Qassar from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa from Isa ibn Qirtas from Zayd al-Qassar from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: We were with him in the mosque, and he spoke to us for a while, then said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Abd Allah ibn Masud taught me a sura to recite, and Zayd taught it to me, and Ubayy taught it to me, and their recitations differed; so whose recitation should I adopt? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was beside him. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Let every person recite as he was taught; each is good and beautiful."
"5085","Hawt al-Abdi from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Salm ibn Junada from Zayd ibn al-Hubab from al-Masudi, who related to me from Hawt al-Abdi who said: I asked Zayd ibn Arqam about the Night of Decree, and he said: I have no doubt and no uncertainty that it is the night of the seventeenth, the night the Quran was sent down and the day the two hosts met."
"5086","Abu al-Waqqas from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, who said: Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Abu Amir al-Aqadi from Ibrahim ibn Tahman from Abd al-Ala from Abu al-Numan from Abu Waqqas from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""When a man promises his brother, intending to fulfill it for him, but does not come to the appointment, there is no sin upon him."""
"5087","Muraqqa al-Tamimi from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Mindal ibn Ali, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Jarir from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym from Muraqqa al-Tamimi who said: I prayed with Zayd ibn Arqam over a funeral and he said the takbir five times, then said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said the takbir five times, so I will not abandon them for anyone after him."
"5088","Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh, who related to me from his father, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Muhammad ibn Jafar, who said: Narrated Shuba from al-Hakam from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi who said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul say: ""Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse."" So I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and Ibn Ubayy came to him and swore to him that he had not said it. The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then came to me and blamed me. I went to my dwelling and slept, as if grieved. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me, so I went to him, and he said: ""Allah has confirmed you as truthful and excused you,"" and he recited these two verses: ""They are the ones who say: Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah,"" until he completed the two verses."
"5089","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Harun ibn Ishaq al-Hamdani from al-Muharibi from Sallam ibn Miskin from one who related to him from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his father or his mother, that suffices for him and for them."""
"5090","Amr ibn Dinar al-Makki from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Shababa from al-Mughira ibn Muslim from Amr ibn Dinar from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A woman does not fulfill the right of Allah upon her until she fulfills the right of her husband, even if he asks her while she is on the back of a camel saddle, she must not withhold herself from him."""
"5091","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani, who said: Narrated Abu Muawiya from Asim from Abu Uthman and Abd Allah ibn al-Harith from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: I will not tell you except what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, miserliness, cowardice, extreme old age, and the punishment of the grave. O Allah, grant my soul its piety; You are the best of those who purify it; You are its Guardian and Master. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, a soul that is never satisfied, a heart that does not humble itself, and a supplication that is not answered."""
"5092","Narrated al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, who said: Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa from Hasan ibn Salih from Asim from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, extreme old age, and the punishment of the grave. O Allah, grant my soul its piety; You are the best of those who purify it; You are its Guardian and Master. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a heart that does not humble itself, a soul that is never satisfied, a prayer that does not benefit, and a supplication that is not answered."""
"5093","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Ali ibn Mushir from Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Uthman from Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5094","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Abu Usama from al-Muthanna ibn Sad Abi Ghifar al-Tai from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith who said: We said to Zayd ibn Arqam: Narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity and laziness, cowardice and miserliness, extreme old age, the punishment of the grave, and the tribulation of the Dajjal. O Allah, grant my soul its piety; You are the best of those who purify it; You are its Guardian and Master. My Lord, I seek refuge in You from a heart that does not humble itself, knowledge that does not benefit, and a supplication that is not heard,"" or he said: ""a supplication that is not answered."""
"5095","Salih Abu al-Khalil from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri, who related to me from his father from his father from his grandfather from Amr ibn al-Harith from Umar ibn Qays from Ata from Abu al-Khalil from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about fasting on Arafa. He said: ""It expiates the year you are in and the year after it."""
"5096","Maymun Abu Abd Allah from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Shuba from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Maymun Abi Abd Allah from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Treat pleurisy with Indian costus and olive oil."""
"5097","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Muadh ibn Hisham, who related to me from his father from Qatada from Maymun Abi Abd Allah from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5098","Narrated Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Baghdadi from Affan from Abu Awana from Mughira from Abu Ubayda from Maymun Abi Abd Allah who said: Zayd ibn Arqam said, as I was listening: We stopped with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a valley called Wadi Khumm. He ordered the prayer and prayed it at midday heat, then addressed us, and shade was made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a garment over a tree from the sun. He said: ""Do you not know that I have more authority over every believing man and woman than their own selves?"" They said: Yes indeed. He said: ""So whomever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."""
"5099","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Sayrafi from Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maymun, who related to me from his father who said: I asked Zayd ibn Arqam what the name of the mother of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was. He said: ""Amina bint Wahb."""
"5100","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib from Hawdha ibn Khalifa from Awf, and narrated Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti from Wahb ibn Baqiyya, who informed us from Khalid from Awf from Maymun Abi Abd Allah from al-Bara ibn Azib and Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali when he intended to go on a campaign: ""One of us must stay behind, either you or I,"" so he left him behind. Some people said: He only left him behind for something he disliked in him. That reached Ali, so he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he laughed and then said: ""O Ali, are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?"""
"5101","Narrated Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Salim al-Qazzaz al-Kufi who said: I found in the book of my father: Narrated Yahya ibn Yala from Sulayman ibn Qarm from Harun ibn Sad from Maymun Abi Abd Allah from Zayd ibn Arqam and al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: ""Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa?"""
"5102","Abu Harun al-Abdi from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Jumhur ibn Mansur from Khalaf ibn Khalifa who said: I heard Abu Harun mention from Zayd ibn Arqam that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Ghadir Khumm: ""Whomever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla."""
"5103","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani from Hammad ibn Zayd from Abu Harun al-Abdi from a man from Zayd ibn Arqam that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali on the day of Ghadir Khumm: ""O Allah, whomever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."""
"5104","Khaythama Abu Nasr al-Basri from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb, who said: Narrated Waki, both from Sufyan from Jabir from Khaythama from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: I complained of my eye, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me and said: ""O Zayd, if your eyes were in the condition they are in, what would you do?"" I said: Then I would be patient and seek reward. He said: ""Then you will meet Allah without any sin."""
"5105","Al-Nadr ibn Anas from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi, who said: Narrated Amr ibn Marzuq, who informed us from Shuba from Qatada from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""These privies are attended by devils, so when one of you enters the lavatory, let him say: I seek refuge in Allah from the impure filth, the accursed Satan."""
"5106","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, and narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar from Muammal ibn Hisham, who said: Narrated Ismail ibn Ibrahim from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""These privies are attended by devils, so when one of you intends to enter, let him say: I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils."""
"5107","Narrated Uthman ibn Amr al-Dabbi and Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Adawi al-Basri, who said: Narrated Amr ibn Marzuq, who informed us from Shuba from Qatada from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Zayd ibn Arqam that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the children of the Ansar."""
"5108","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, and narrated Jafar ibn Ahmad al-Shami al-Kufi from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, who related to me from his father from Ibrahim ibn Tahman from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj from Qatada from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar."""
"5109","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Shuja ibn Makhlad from Hushaym from Ali ibn Zayd, who related to us from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the offspring of the Ansar, and the offspring of their offspring."""
"5110","Abu Bakr ibn Anas from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Yazid ibn Harun, who informed us from Hammad ibn Salama from Thabit from Abu Bakr ibn Anas who said: Zayd ibn Arqam wrote to Anas ibn Malik consoling him for his children and family who were afflicted at al-Harra, and wrote in his letter: And I give you glad tidings of gladness from Allah; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar, and the women of the Ansar, and the women of the children of the Ansar, and the women of the children of the children of the Ansar."""
"5111","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, who related to me from his father from Yazid ibn Harun, who informed us from Hammad ibn Salama from Ali ibn Zayd from Abu Bakr ibn Anas from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"5112","Narrated Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi from Fahd ibn Awf Abu Rabia from Hammad ibn Salama from Ali ibn Zayd from Abu Bakr ibn Anas who said: Zayd ibn Arqam wrote to Anas ibn Malik consoling him for those of his people and family who were afflicted on the day of al-Harra, and wrote: I give you glad tidings of gladness from Allah; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar, and the women of the Ansar, and the women of the children of the Ansar, and the women of the children of the children of the Ansar."""
"5113","Thabit ibn Mirdas from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughba from Said ibn Ufayr from Sulayman ibn Bilal from Haram ibn Uthman from Abu Atiq from Thabit ibn Mirdas from Zayd ibn Arqam: When Ibn Ziyad was brought the head of al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, he began tapping with a stick in his hand upon his eye and nose. Zayd said to him: Lift the stick, for I have seen the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in its place."
"5114","Al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Khalid ibn Nizar from Ibrahim ibn Tahman from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj from Qatada from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The prayer of the oft-returning is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun."""
"5115","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa from Abu Marzuq from Qatada from al-Qasim ibn Awf from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by the mosque of Quba while they were praying two rakas, and said: ""What is this prayer?"" They said: Glorification. He said: ""The prayer of the oft-returning is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun."""
"5116","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Khalid ibn Nizar from Ibrahim ibn Tahman from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj from Qatada from al-Qasim ibn Awf from Zayd ibn Arqam that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by them while they were praying Duha when the sun had risen, and said: ""The prayer of the oft-returning is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun."""
"5117","Narrated Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from Yazid ibn Zuray from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque of Quba while they were praying when the sun had risen, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The prayer of the oft-returning, they used to pray it when the young camels feel the heat of the sun."""
"5118","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from Musa ibn Dawud, and narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Naqid al-Basri from Musa ibn Harun al-Mustamli, who related to us from Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi from Husam ibn Misakk from Qatada from al-Qasim al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque of Quba and saw them praying Duha, and said: ""This is the prayer of the oft-returning."""
"5119","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Waki from Hisham al-Dastuwai from Qatada from al-Qasim al-Shaybani from Zayd who said: He went out to the people of Quba while they were praying Duha, and said: ""The prayer of the oft-returning is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun,"" and he did not raise it to the Prophet."
"5120","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri from Abu al-Jumahir Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Tunukhi from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""These privies are attended by devils, so when one of you enters them, let him say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils."""
"5121","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani, who said: Narrated Abda ibn Sulayman, and narrated Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, and narrated Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, who said: Narrated Yazid ibn Zuray, who said: Narrated Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""These privies are attended by devils, so when one of you intends to enter, let him say: I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils."""
"5122","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Ahmad ibn Hafs, who related to me from his father from Ibrahim ibn Tahman from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj from Qatada from al-Qasim al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam that Muadh said: O Messenger of Allah, do you see the People of the Book prostrating to their bishops and patriarchs! Should we not prostrate to you? He said: ""If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command a woman to prostrate to her husband; and a woman does not fulfill the right of her husband until, if he asks her for herself even on a camel saddle, she gives it to him."""
"5123","Narrated Ahmad ibn Masud from Amr ibn Abi Salama, and narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi who said: Narrated Amr ibn Abi Salama from Sadaqa from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Qasim ibn Awf from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Muadh to Syria. When he returned he said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw the People of the Book prostrating to their bishops and patriarchs; should we not prostrate to you? He said: ""If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command a woman to prostrate to her husband; and a woman does not fulfill the right of her husband until, if he asks her for herself on the back of a camel saddle, she gives it to him."""
"5124","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi from Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni from Sahl ibn Husam ibn Misakk, who related to me from his father from Qatada from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What an excellent man Bilal is, and the muadhins will have the longest necks among people."""
"5125","Al-Qasim ibn Rabia from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, who said: Narrated al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani from Yazid ibn Harun, who informed us from Husam ibn Misakk from Qatada from al-Qasim ibn Rabia from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What an excellent man Bilal is; none but a believer follows him, and he is the chief of the muadhins, and the muadhins will have the longest necks among people on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5126","Iyas ibn Abi Ramla al-Shami from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Kathir from Israil from Uthman ibn al-Mughira from Iyas ibn Abi Ramla al-Shami who said: I witnessed Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him, asking Zayd ibn Arqam: Did you witness with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two Eids coinciding on one day? He said: Yes. He said: Then what did he do? He said: He prayed the Eid, then gave concession regarding Friday, saying: ""Whoever wishes, let him pray."""
"5127","Thabit ibn Mirdas from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Umari al-Qadi from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah al-Uwaysi from Sulayman ibn Bilal from Haram ibn Uthman from Thabit ibn Mirdas from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: Ibn Ziyad was brought the head of al-Husayn, and he began placing a stick in his hand upon his eye and nose. Zayd ibn Arqam said: ""Lift the stick."" He said: Why? He said: I saw the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in its place."
"5128","Abu Muslim al-Bajali from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, who informed us from Mutamir ibn Sulayman, who related to us from Dawud al-Tufawi who said: Abu Muslim al-Bajali related to me from Zayd ibn Arqam that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at the end of the prayer: ""O Allah, You are our Lord and the Lord of all things; I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger. O Allah, You are our Lord and the Lord of all things; I bear witness that all servants are brothers. O Allah, You are our Lord and the Lord of all things; make me devoted to You, me and my family, in this world and the Hereafter. O Possessor of majesty and honor, hear and answer. Allah is the Greatest, the Greatest. O Allah, You are the light of the heavens and the earth. Allah is the Greatest, the Greatest. Allah is sufficient for me, and He is the best Disposer of affairs. Allah is the Greatest, the Greatest."""
"5129","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, who informed us from Mutamir ibn Sulayman who said: I heard Dawud al-Tufawi say: Abu Muslim al-Bajali related to me from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: Some Bedouin people came and said: Let us go to this man; if he is a prophet, then we are the most fortunate of people by him, and if he is a king, we will live under his wing! So I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what they said. Then they came to the chambers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began calling out: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! Then Allah the Almighty revealed: ""Indeed those who call out to you from behind the chambers, most of them do not understand."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of my ear and said: ""Allah has confirmed your word as true, O Zayd."""
"5130","Abd Allah ibn Zayd ibn Arqam from his father. Narrated Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri from Abd al-Munim ibn Bashir al-Ansari from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Anasi, of the descendants of Anas, from Abd Allah ibn Zayd ibn Arqam from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Whoever says at the end of every prayer: 'Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of might, above what they describe, and peace be upon the messengers, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds,' three times, has measured out the fullest measure of reward."""
"5131","Unaysa bint Zayd ibn Arqam from her father. Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Said ibn Sulayman, and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani, who said: Narrated Abbad ibn al-Awwam from Said ibn Abi Aruba, who informed me from Thabit ibn Zayd ibn Thabit ibn Zayd ibn Arqam, who related to me from my paternal aunt Unaysa bint Zayd ibn Arqam from her father Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Gold and silk are lawful for the females of my umma and forbidden for its males."""
"5132","Narrated Musa ibn Harun and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, who said: Narrated Umayya ibn Bistam from Mutamir ibn Sulayman, who related to us from Nubata bint Burayr from Hamada from Unaysa bint Zayd ibn Arqam from her father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Zayd ibn Arqam during an illness he had, and said: ""There is no harm upon you from this illness of yours, but how will you be when you live long after me and become blind?"" He said: Then I will be patient and seek reward. He said: ""Then you will enter Paradise without reckoning."" He became blind after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, then Allah restored his sight to him, then he died, may Allah have mercy on him."
"5133","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Umayya ibn Bistam from Mutamir ibn Sulayman, who informed us from Thabit ibn Zayd from Azhar from Unaysa bint Zayd ibn Arqam, that Zayd visited al-Mukhtar and said: O Abu Amir, if you had preceded, you would have seen Jibril and Mikail! He said: You have dug and pecked; you are more insignificant to Allah than I am; that one is a liar who fabricates against Allah and His Messenger."
"5134","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan from Salama ibn al-Fadl from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Habib ibn Zayd ibn Khallad al-Ansari from Unaysa bint Zayd ibn Arqam from her father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that the trees be cleared of what was beneath them and sprinkled, then addressed us. By Allah, there is nothing that will occur until the Hour comes except that he informed us of it that day. Then he said: ""O people, who has more authority over you than your own selves?"" We said: Allah and His Messenger have more authority over us than our own selves. He said: ""So whomever I am his mawla, then this one is his mawla,"" meaning Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Then he took him by the hand and raised it, then said: ""O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."""
"5135","Umm Mabad from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Amr ibn Awf, who informed us from Khalid, and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Musa ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, both from Yahya al-Jabir from Umm Mabad from Zayd ibn Arqam and Qaraza ibn Kab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gourds, varnished vessels, and hollowed stumps."
"5136","An unnamed man from Zayd ibn Arqam. Narrated Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi from Umayya ibn Bistam from Mutamir ibn Sulayman, who related to us from Thabit ibn Zayd from a man from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Allah the Almighty loves silence on three occasions: at the recitation of the Quran, at the battlefront, and at the funeral."""
"5137","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr say: ""Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi is Zayd ibn al-Numan."""
"5138","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from Mansur from Mujahid from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Usfan, and the polytheists faced us under Khalid ibn al-Walid, between us and the qibla. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Zuhr. They said: They were in a state where, had we seized their unguardedness! They said: There will now come upon them a prayer dearer to them than their children and their own selves! Then Jibril, peace be upon him, came down with these verses between Zuhr and Asr: ""And when you are among them and establish the prayer for them."" He said: The time of prayer came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them and they took up arms. We lined up behind him in two rows, then he bowed and we all bowed, then he raised his head and we all raised, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated with the row next to him while the others stood guarding them. When they prostrated and stood, the others sat and prostrated in their place. Then these advanced to the positions of those, and those came to the positions of these, and they bowed together, then raised and all raised, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated with the row next to him while the others stood guarding them. When they sat, the others sat and prostrated, then he gave salam to them and turned away. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed it twice: once at Usfan, and once in the land of Banu Sulaym."
"5139","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Muawiya ibn Amr from Zaida from Mansur from Mujahid from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Usfan, and the polytheists faced us under Khalid ibn al-Walid, between us and the qibla. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Zuhr. They said: They were in a state where, had we seized their unguardedness! They said: There will now come upon them a prayer dearer to them than their children and their own selves! Then Jibril came down with these verses between Zuhr and Asr: ""And when you are among them and establish the prayer for them."" He said: The time of prayer came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them and they took up arms. We lined up behind him in two rows, then he bowed and we all bowed, then he raised his head and we all raised, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated with the row next to him, while the others stood guarding them. When they prostrated and stood, the others sat and prostrated, then he gave salam to them and turned away. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed it twice: once at Usfan, and once in the land of Banu Sulaym."
"5140","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, who related to me from his father from Muhammad ibn Jafar, and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Ghundar from Shuba from Mansur from Mujahid from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was arrayed facing the enemy at Usfan with Khalid ibn al-Walid over the polytheists. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in Zuhr, then the polytheists said: They have a prayer dearer to them than their wealth and children. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them, lining them in two rows behind him, the prayer of fear. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed with all of them; when they raised their heads, the row next to him prostrated while the others stood. When they raised their heads from prostration, the rear row prostrated along with their bowing with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the front row stepped back and the rear row stepped forward, and each one stood in the position of the other. Then he bowed and the others stood; when they finished their prostrations, the others prostrated, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam to them."
"5141","Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Yahya ibn Hamza from Dawud ibn Isa al-Kufi, who related to us from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, who related to me from Mujahid ibn Jabr al-Makki, who related to us from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi who said: We campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the polytheists met him at Usfan with Khalid ibn al-Walid over their cavalry that day. The Zuhr prayer came upon us, and the caller to prayer called and the iqama was given. The polytheists intended to charge at us, but some of them said: There will soon come upon them a prayer dearer to them than their children, meaning the Asr prayer. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him with the verses containing the prayer of fear. When the prayer time came, the caller called and the iqama was given, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and we lined up behind him in two rows, with the polytheists that day on the side of the qibla. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed and we bowed, then he prostrated and the row next to him prostrated, while the rear stood. When they finished their prostrations, the rear row prostrated, and the polytheists blamed one another among themselves. Abu Ayyash said: He also prayed with us likewise in the land of Banu Sulaym."
"5142","Narrated Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqa from Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khali al-Himsi, who related to me from his father from Salama ibn Abd al-Malik al-Awsi, who related to us from Abu al-Hasan al-Hamdani, meaning Ali ibn Salih, from Mansur from Mujahid from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the prayer of fear: that he prayed with the people and they all bowed, then all raised; some of them prostrated with him while the others stood. When they raised their heads, they stepped back and the others came and some of them prostrated with him while the others stood. When they raised their heads, they stepped back and the others came and prostrated in their place. Then he prayed the second as the first, then sat, and those next to him sat while the others stood, then he gave salam and those next to him gave salam, then they stood and those others came and prostrated in their place, then gave salam."
"5143","Narrated Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti, who related to me from his father from Yazid ibn Harun, who informed us from Jafar ibn al-Harith from Mansur from Mujahid from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Zuhr prayer at Usfan, with Khalid ibn al-Walid over the polytheists. The polytheists said: They were in a state where, had we seized their unguardedness! They said: There will now come upon them a prayer dearer to them than their children and their own selves! Then Jibril, peace be upon him, came down with the verses containing the prayer of fear. He lined his Companions behind him in two rows; he said the takbir and we all said the takbir, he bowed and we all bowed, he prostrated and the row next to him prostrated. When he stood, the row next to him stepped back and stood in the position of the rear row, and the rear row stepped forward and stood in their position. He bowed and we all bowed, raised and we all raised, and the row next to him prostrated; when he sat, the rear row prostrated."
"5144","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Usayd al-Asbahani from Yunus ibn Habib from Abu Dawud from Warqa from Mansur from Mujahid from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Usfan, and the time of prayer, the Zuhr prayer, came, with Khalid ibn al-Walid over the cavalry of the polytheists. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led his Companions in Zuhr. The polytheists said: They have a prayer after this dearer to them than their children, wealth, and selves, meaning the Asr prayer. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, came down upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between Zuhr and Asr and informed him, and this verse was revealed: ""And when you are among them and establish the prayer for them,"" to its end. The time of prayer came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lined his Companions in two rows with their arms upon them, and the enemy before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They all said the takbir and all bowed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated along with the row next to him, while the others stood guarding them. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he stood for the second raka and the others prostrated. Then these advanced to the positions of those, and those stepped back to the positions of these, and he prayed with them the other raka; they all bowed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated along with the row next to him, while the others stood guarding them. When they finished, these prostrated, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam. Abu Ayyash said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed this prayer twice: once at Usfan, and once in the land of Banu Sulaym."
"5145","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa from Israil from Mansur from Mujahid from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Zuhr prayer at Usfan. When he finished, the polytheists, with Khalid ibn al-Walid over them, said: They were in a state where, had we wished, we would have caught them unawares and seized their unguardedness! Then this verse was revealed between Zuhr and Asr concerning the prayer, and he mentioned similar to it."
"5146","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh from Said ibn Mansur from Jarir from Mansur from Mujahid from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer, and he mentioned the like of it."
"5147","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, who said: Narrated Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Hammad ibn Salama from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things, it will be for him as the freeing of a slave from the descendants of Ismail, ten good deeds will be recorded for him, ten evil deeds will be erased from him, he will be raised ten degrees, and he will be in protection from Satan until evening. If he says it in the evening, he will have the like of that."" He said: A man then saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a dream and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi informed us from you of such-and-such! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Abu Ayyash has spoken the truth."""
"5148","Zayd ibn Kharija al-Ansari, of Banu Haritha ibn al-Khazraj, a Badri; he used to reside in Medina and died during the caliphate of Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father from Muawiya ibn Hisham from Sufyan from Humran ibn Ayan from Abu al-Tufayl from Ibn Kharija, and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi from Abthar ibn al-Qasim from Humran ibn Ayan from Abu al-Tufayl from Ibn Kharija who said: When news of the death of al-Najashi reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Your brother has died."" He went out, and we lined up behind him and prayed, though we saw nothing."
"5149","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Musa ibn Ismail from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, and narrated Abu Khalifa from Ali ibn al-Madini from Marwan ibn Muawiya al-Fazari, who said: Narrated Uthman ibn Hakim from Khalid ibn Salama from Musa ibn Talha from Zayd ibn Kharija al-Ansari who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, we know how to greet you with salam, but how do we invoke blessings upon you? He said: ""Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."""
"5150","Narrated al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani from al-Dahhak ibn Maymun al-Thaqafi from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Zayd or Yazid ibn Nafi from Habib ibn Salim from al-Numan ibn Bashir who said: While Zayd ibn Kharija was walking on one of the roads of Medina, he fell dead between Zuhr and Asr. He was carried to his family and covered between two cloaks and a garment. Between Maghrib and Isha, a group of Ansari women gathered wailing around him, when they heard a voice from beneath the covering saying: ""Be silent, O people,"" twice. They uncovered his face and chest, and he said: ""Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the unlettered Prophet, the seal of the prophets; that was in the first Book."" Then it was said upon his tongue: ""Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, the successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the strong, the trustworthy, has spoken the truth; he was weak in body, strong in the command of Allah; that was in the first Book."" Then it was said upon his tongue: ""He has spoken the truth, he has spoken the truth,"" three times, ""and the middle one, the servant of Allah, Umar, the Commander of the Believers, who did not fear in the cause of Allah the blame of any blamer, and who prevented people so their strong would not devour their weak; that was in the first Book."" Then it was said upon his tongue: ""He has spoken the truth, he has spoken the truth, he has spoken the truth."" Then he said: ""Uthman, the Commander of the Believers, merciful to the believers; two have passed and four remain. Then people will differ and have no order, and the sanctuaries will be made lawful, meaning the sacred bounds will be violated, the Hour will draw near, and people will devour one another."""
"5151","Narrated Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar al-Wasiti from Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan from Ishaq al-Azraq from Sharik from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir from Habib ibn Salim from al-Numan ibn Bashir who said: When Zayd ibn Kharija died, his burial was awaited until Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, came out. I said: He prays two rakas, then he uncovered the garment from his face and said: Peace be upon you, peace be upon you. The people of the household were speaking. I said, while in prayer: Glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah. Then he said: ""Be silent, be silent. Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; that was in the first Book. He has spoken the truth, he has spoken the truth, he has spoken the truth. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, weak in body, strong in the command of Allah; that was in the first Book. He has spoken the truth, he has spoken the truth, he has spoken the truth. Umar ibn al-Khattab, strong in body, strong in the command of Allah; that was in the first Book. He has spoken the truth, he has spoken the truth, he has spoken the truth. Uthman ibn Affan: two have passed and four remain, and the sanctuaries have been made lawful. The well of Aris, and what is the well of Aris! Peace be upon you, Abd Allah ibn Rawaha. Have Kharija and Sad perceived me?"" Sharik said: They are his father and his brother."
"5152","Zayd ibn Abi Awfa al-Aslami; he used to reside in Basra. Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Nasr ibn Ali from Abd al-Mumin ibn Abbad ibn Amr al-Abdi from Yazid ibn Man, who related to me from Abd Allah ibn Shurahbil from a man of Quraysh from Zayd ibn Abi Awfa who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque of Medina, and he began saying: ""Where is so-and-so son of so-and-so?"" He kept checking on them and sending for them until they gathered with him. He said: ""I will relate to you a hadith, so memorize it, comprehend it, and relate it to those after you. Allah chose from His creation a creation."" Then he recited this verse: ""Allah chooses messengers from the angels and from people,"" a creation He admits into Paradise. And I choose from you whom I love to choose, and I establish brotherhood among you as Allah established brotherhood among the angels. Stand, O Abu Bakr."" He stood and knelt before him. He said: ""You have a favor with me; Allah will reward you for it. Had I taken a close friend, I would have taken you as a close friend; you are to me in the position of my shirt to my body."" And he moved his shirt with his hand. Then he said: ""Come near, O Umar."" He came near, and he said: ""You were severely troublesome toward us, O Abu Hafs, so I supplicated to Allah to strengthen the religion through you or through Abu Jahl, and Allah did that through you, and you were the dearer of the two to me. You are with me in Paradise, the third of three from this umma."" Then he stepped aside and established brotherhood between him and Abu Bakr. Then he called Uthman and said: ""Come near, O Uthman, come near, O Uthman."" He kept drawing near until he pressed his knee against the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he looked at him, then looked to the sky and said: ""Glory be to Allah the Magnificent,"" three times. Then he looked at Uthman, and his buttons were undone, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) buttoned them with his hand. Then he said: ""Gather the two ends of your cloak upon your neck, for you have a station among the people of heaven. You are among those who will come to me at the Hawd with your jugular veins gushing blood. I will say: Who did this to you? And you will say: So-and-so and so-and-so. That is the speech of Jibril, peace be upon him, when he called out from heaven: Verily Uthman is trustworthy against every forsaker."" Then he called Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and said: ""Come near, O trustworthy one of Allah; and the trustworthy one in heaven, Allah will give you mastery over your wealth in truth. You have a supplication with me, and I have deferred it."" He said: Choose for me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""You have entrusted me, O Abd al-Rahman, with a trust; may Allah increase your wealth."" And he kept moving his hand. Then he stepped aside and established brotherhood between him and Uthman. Then Talha and al-Zubayr entered, and he said: ""Draw near to me."" They drew near to him, and he said: ""You two are my disciples, like the disciples of Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon him."" Then he established brotherhood between them. Then he called Sad ibn Abi Waqqas and Ammar ibn Yasir and said: ""O Ammar, the rebellious party will kill you."" Then he established brotherhood between them. Then he called Uwaymir Abu al-Darda and Salman al-Farisi and said: ""O Salman, you are of us, the People of the House, and Allah has given you the first knowledge and the last knowledge, the first Book and the last Book."" Then he said: ""Shall I not guide you, O Abu al-Darda?"" He said: Yes indeed, may my father and mother be ransomed for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""If you rescue them, they will rescue you; if you abandon them, they will not abandon you; if you flee from them, they will catch you. So lend them your honor for the day of your need."" Then he established brotherhood between them. Then he looked at the faces of his Companions and said: ""Rejoice and be comforted, for you are the first who will come to me at the Hawd, and you are in the highest chambers."" Then he looked at Abd Allah ibn Umar and said: ""Praise be to Allah Who guides from misguidance."" Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, my spirit has departed and my back has broken when I saw you do what you did with your Companions apart from me. If it is due to anger toward me, then to you belong satisfaction and honor. He said: ""By the One Who sent me with the truth, I only kept you back for myself. You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, and my heir."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do I inherit from you? He said: ""What the prophets bequeathed."" He said: And what did the prophets before you bequeath? He said: ""The Book of Allah and the sunna of their Prophet. And you are with me in my palace in Paradise, with Fatima my daughter, and my companion."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the verse: ""Brothers, upon couches facing one another."" The friends in Allah, looking at one another."
"5153","Zayd ibn Sana; he died in the campaign of Tabuk. Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti from his father, and narrated Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani from al-Walid ibn Muslim from Muhammad ibn Hamza ibn Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam from his father from his grandfather from Abd Allah ibn Salam who said: When Allah intended the guidance of Zayd ibn Sana, Zayd ibn Sana said: There is no sign of prophethood except that I recognized it in the face of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I looked at him, except two that I had not yet tested in him: that his forbearance precedes his anger, and that severity of provocation only increases him in forbearance. I sought subtle means to associate with him so I might know his forbearance from his anger. Zayd ibn Sana said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day from the chambers with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him. A man came to him on his mount like a Bedouin and said: O Messenger of Allah, Busra, the village of Banu so-and-so, have embraced Islam and entered it, and I had told them that if they embraced Islam, provision would come to them in abundance. But a year of drought, hardship, and lack of rain has struck them, and I fear, O Messenger of Allah, that they will leave Islam out of greed just as they entered it out of greed. If you see fit to send them something to aid them with, do so! He looked at a man beside him, I think it was Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: O Messenger of Allah, nothing of it remains. Zayd ibn Sana said: I drew near to him and said: O Muhammad, will you sell me known dates from the orchard of Banu so-and-so until such-and-such a term? He said: ""No, O Jew, but I will sell you known dates until such-and-such a term, without naming the orchard of Banu so-and-so."" I said: Yes. So he transacted with me, and I loosened my purse and gave him eighty mithqals of gold for known dates until such-and-such a term. He gave it to the man and said: ""Go to them in the morning and aid them with it."" Zayd ibn Sana said: Two or three days before the term fell due, I came to him, seized the folds of his shirt and cloak, and looked at him with a stern face, saying to him: Will you not pay me my due, O Muhammad? By Allah, I have only known you, Banu Abd al-Muttalib, as delayers! And I had knowledge through associating with you. I looked at Umar, and his eyes were rolling in his face like the revolving celestial sphere. Then he cast his gaze at me and said: O enemy of Allah, do you say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what I hear, and do to him what I see! By the One Who sent him with the truth, were it not that I fear missing him, I would strike your head with my sword. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Umar calmly and gently, then said: ""O Umar, he and I needed something other than this: that you command me to repay well and command him to pursue well. Go with him, O Umar, and give him his due, and add twenty sas of dates in place of having frightened him."" Zayd said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, went with me and gave me my due, adding twenty sas of dates. I said: What is this addition, O Umar? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to add to you in place of having frightened you. I said: Do you know me, O Umar? He said: No; who are you? I said: I am Zayd ibn Sana. He said: The scholar? I said: The scholar. He said: Then what moved you to do to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what you did, and say to him what you said? I said: O Umar, there was no sign of prophethood except that I recognized it in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I looked at him, except two that I had not tested in him: that his forbearance precedes his anger, and that provocation only increases him in forbearance. I have now tested them. I call you to witness, O Umar, that I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet. And I call you to witness that half my wealth, and I am among the wealthiest of them, is charity upon the umma of Muhammad. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Or upon some of them, for you cannot encompass them all. I said: Or upon some of them. Then Umar and Zayd returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Zayd said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He believed in him, affirmed him, pledged allegiance to him, and witnessed many campaigns with him. Then Zayd died in the campaign of Tabuk, advancing and not retreating. May Allah have mercy on Zayd."
"5154","Zayd ibn Jariya al-Ansari, of his reports. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Kalbi from Sayfi ibn Ribi from Uthman ibn Ubayd Allah from Jamil ibn Zayd who said: I saw five of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing gold rings, among them Zayd ibn Jariya, Zayd ibn Arqam, al-Bara ibn Azib, Anas ibn Malik, and Abd Allah ibn Yazid."
"5155","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi from Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran from his father who said: It was said to Ibn Umar: Zayd ibn Jariya has died. He said: ""May Allah have mercy on him."" It was said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, he left a hundred thousand! He said: ""But it has not left him."""
"5156","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Abi Attab Abu Bakr al-Ayan from Mansur ibn Salama Abu Salama al-Khuzai from Uthman ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Zayd ibn Jariya, who related to me from my father Ubayd Allah ibn Zayd, who related to me from my father Zayd ibn Jariya who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) deemed some people too young on the day of Uhud, among them Zayd ibn Jariya, meaning himself, al-Bara ibn Azib, Sad ibn Khaythama, Abu Said al-Khudri, Abd Allah ibn Umar, and Jabir ibn Abd Allah."
"5157","Zayd ibn Ishaq al-Ansari; he used to reside in Egypt. Narrated Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri from Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from Ibn Lahia from Zayd ibn Ishaq al-Ansari who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me at the door of the mosque and said: ""Shall I not guide you to a treasure among the treasures of Paradise?"" I said: Yes indeed, O Prophet of Allah. He said: ""There is no power nor strength except through Allah."""
"5158","Zayd ibn Aslam ibn Thalaba ibn Adi ibn al-Ajlan al-Ansari, a Badri. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, who related to me from his father from Ibn Lahia from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar: Zayd ibn Aslam ibn Thalaba ibn Adi ibn al-Ajlan."
"5159","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from al-Aws, then from Banu al-Ajlan: Zayd ibn Aslam ibn Thalaba."
"5160","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Dirar ibn Surad from Ali ibn Hashim from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi from his father, regarding the naming of those who were with Ali: Zayd ibn Aslam of the Ansar, a Badri."
"5161","Zayd ibn Rabia al-Qurashi, of Banu Asad ibn Abd al-Rahman. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, who related to me from his father from Ibn Lahia from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa who said: ""And there were killed on the day of Hunayn among the Muslims, of Quraysh, then of Banu Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza: Zayd ibn Rabia."""
"5162","Zayd ibn Ruqaysh, an ally of Banu Umayya ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf; he was martyred on the day of Yamama. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, who related to me from his father from Ibn Lahia from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those killed on the day of Yamama among the Muslims: Zayd ibn Ruqaysh, an ally of Banu Umayya."
"5163","Zayd ibn Suraqa ibn Kab al-Ansari; he was killed on the day of the Bridge with Sad ibn Abi Waqqas in the year fifteen. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, who related to me from his father from Ibn Lahia from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those killed on the day of the Bridge, the bridge of al-Madain, with Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, of the Ansar, then of Banu al-Najjar: Zayd ibn Suraqa ibn Kab."
"5164","Zayd ibn al-Muzayyan al-Ansari, a Badri. Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr of the Ansar, then of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Zayd ibn al-Muzayyan."
"5165","Zayd ibn Wadia ibn Amr al-Ansari, a Badri. Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr of the Ansar, then of Banu Awf ibn al-Khazraj of Bilhubla: Zayd ibn Wadia ibn Amr ibn Qays."
"5166","Zayd ibn Usayd ibn Jariya al-Zuhri; he was martyred on the day of Yamama. Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Yamama of Quraysh, then of Banu Zuhra: Zayd ibn Usayd ibn Jariya."
"5167","Zayd ibn Labid al-Ansari, an Aqabi. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, who related to me from his father from Ibn Lahia from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those who attended al-Aqaba of the Ansar, then of Banu Bayada: Zayd ibn Labid."
"5168","Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, kunya Abu Talha; also said Abu Muhammad, also said Abu Abd al-Rahman; he used to reside in Medina, and died there. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr say: ""Zayd ibn Khalid has the kunya Abu Abd al-Rahman."""
"5169","Narrated Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj from Yahya ibn Bukayr who said: ""Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani died in the year seventy-eight, with the kunya Abu Abd al-Rahman, at the age of eighty-five."""
"5170","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, who said: Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr who said: ""Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani died, with the kunya Abu Muhammad, in the year seventy-eight."""
"5171","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Madini who said: ""It was said the kunya of Zayd ibn Khalid was Abu Talha."""
"5172","Al-Saib ibn Yazid from Zayd ibn Khalid. Narrated al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari from Amr ibn Abi Asim, who related to me from his father from Ibn Jurayj from Abu Said al-Ama from al-Saib ibn Yazid from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saw him praying after Asr and struck him with the stick while he continued praying as he was. When he finished he said: ""By Allah, O Commander of the Believers, I will not abandon it after I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray it."""
"5173","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Jurayj from Abu Said al-Ama from al-Saib ibn Yazid from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that he said to Umar ibn al-Khattab regarding the two rakas after Asr: I will not abandon them after I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray them."
"5174","Al-Saib ibn Khallad al-Ansari from Zayd ibn Khalid. Narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi from Qabisa ibn Uqba from Sufyan from Abd Allah ibn Abi Labid from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab from Khallad ibn al-Saib from his father from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Jibril came to me and said to me: O Muhammad, command your Companions to raise their voices with the talbiya, for it is among the rites of Hajj."""
"5175","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari from Shuayb ibn Ayyub from Muawiya ibn Hisham from Sufyan from Abd Allah ibn Abi Labid from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab from Khallad ibn al-Saib from his father from Zayd ibn Khalid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5176","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, and narrated al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari from Zuhayr ibn Harb, Khalaf ibn Salim, and Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, who said: Narrated Waki from Sufyan from Abd Allah ibn Abi Labid from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab from Khallad ibn al-Saib from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Jibril came to me and said: Command your Companions to raise their voices with the talbiya, for it is among the rites of Hajj."""
"5177","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Ahmad ibn Yunus from Zuhayr from Musa ibn Uqba, who informed me from Abu al-Mughira of Banu Zuhra from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab from Khallad ibn al-Saib al-Ansari from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah said: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Raise the voice with the ihram call, for it is among the rites of Hajj."""
"5178","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Missisi from Habban ibn Hilal and Yala ibn Asad al-Ammi, who said: Narrated Wuhayb from Musa ibn Uqba, who informed me from Abd Allah ibn Abi Labid from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah from Khallad ibn al-Saib from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Allah commands you to order your Companions to raise their voices with the talbiya, for it is among the rites of Hajj."""
"5179","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Sufyan ibn Uyayna from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr from Khallad ibn al-Saib from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Command your Companions to proclaim the talbiya aloud, for it is among the rites of Hajj,"" and he did not mention Zayd ibn Khalid."
"5180","Abu Amra, freedman of the Ansar, from Zayd ibn Khalid. Narrated Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar from Yazid ibn Harun, who informed us from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban from Abu Amra, freedman of Zayd ibn Khalid, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was called to a funeral to pray over it, and said: ""Your companion misappropriated spoils in the path of Allah."""
"5181","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Jurayj, who informed me from Yahya ibn Said that Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban informed him that Abu Amra, freedman of the Ansar, informed him that he heard Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar, when a man of Ashja died and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over him. They went to look into his belongings and found in them beads of Jewish beads worth two dirhams."
"5182","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qanabi from Malik, and narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi from Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam, and narrated Bakr ibn Sahl from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, who said: Malik informed us from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban from Abu Amra al-Ansari, that Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani informed him that a man died on the day of Khaybar, and they mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Zayd claimed that he said: ""Pray over your companion."" The faces of the people changed at that. Zayd claimed that he said: ""Your companion has misappropriated spoils in the path of Allah."" He said: So we opened his belongings and found beads of Jewish beads worth two dirhams."
"5183","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Ali ibn al-Madini from Sufyan ibn Uyayna from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban from Abu Amra from Zayd ibn Khalid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"5184","Narrated Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza al-Zubayri, who related to me from his father from Abu Damra Anas ibn Iyad from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban from Ibn Abi Amra from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of Ashja died, and they mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""Pray over your companion."" The faces of the people changed at that. When he saw what was in them, he said: ""Your companion misappropriated spoils in the path of Allah."" So we searched his belongings and found beads of Jewish beads not worth two dirhams."
"5185","Narrated Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban from Ibn Abi Amra from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: A man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of Ashja died, and they mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""Pray over your companion, for he has misappropriated spoils in the path of Allah."" So they searched his belongings and found in them beads of Jewish beads not worth two dirhams."
"5186","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Abd Allah ibn Numayr from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban from Abu Amra, that he heard Zayd ibn Khalid narrate that a Muslim man died at Khaybar, and he was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""Pray over your companion."" The faces of the people changed at that. When he saw what was in them, he said: ""Your companion has misappropriated spoils in the path of Allah."" So we searched his belongings and found beads of Jewish beads not worth two dirhams."
"5187","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Jarir from Yazid ibn Harun from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban from Abu Amra, Yazid said: the freedman of Zayd ibn Khalid, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: A man died on the day of Khaybar, and that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""Pray over your companion."" That was hard upon the people and their faces changed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Your companion has misappropriated spoils in the path of Allah."" His belongings were looked into and beads of Jewish beads he had misappropriated were found; by Allah, I do not think they were worth two dirhams!"
"5188","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amra from Zayd ibn Khalid. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qanabi from Malik, and narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam, and narrated Bakr ibn Sahl from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, who said: Malik informed us from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman from Ibn Abi Amra al-Ansari from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Shall I not inform you of the best of witnesses? The one who brings his testimony before he is asked for it, or informs of his testimony before he is asked for it."""
"5189","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, who said: Narrated Zayd ibn al-Hubab, who related to me from Ubayy ibn Abbas ibn Sahl al-Saidi, who informed me from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, who informed me from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, who informed me from Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, who informed me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amra al-Ansari, who informed me from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The best of witnesses is one who delivers his testimony before he is asked about it."""
"5190","Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti from Wahb ibn Baqiyya, who informed us from Khalid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best testimony is what its bearer testifies to before he is asked for it."""
"5191","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, who said: Narrated Abd Allah ibn Idris from Muhammad ibn Umara from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abd Allah ibn Amr from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Shall I not inform you of the best of witnesses? Those who begin with their testimony before they are asked for it."""
"5192","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam from Bakr ibn Mudar from Yazid ibn al-Had from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman from Ibn Abi Amra from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Hospitality is three days; what is beyond that is charity."""
"5193","Narrated Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza al-Zubayri, who related to me from his father from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim from Yazid ibn al-Had from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman from Ibn Abi Amra from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Hospitality is three nights; what is beyond that is charity."""
"5194","Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Zayd ibn Khalid. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, who informed us from Abd al-Razzaq, who informed us from Ibn Jurayj, who informed me from Ibn Shihab from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Abu Hurayra and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a Bedouin man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I adjure you by Allah, judge for me only by the Book of Allah! The other disputant, who was more knowledgeable than him, said: Yes, judge between us by the Book of Allah and permit me! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Speak."" He said: My son was a hired laborer with this one, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son incurred stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they informed us that my son incurs only a hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and that stoning is upon his wife! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will surely judge between you by the Book of Allah. The sheep and the slave girl are returned; your son incurs a hundred lashes and banishment for one year. Go, O Unays,"" to a man of Aslam, ""to the wife of this one; if she confesses, stone her."" So he went to her in the morning and she confessed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding her and she was stoned."
"5195","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Abu Hurayra and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son was a hired laborer with this one, and he committed adultery with his wife. We were told that my son incurred stoning, so I ransomed him with a slave girl and a hundred sheep. Then the people of knowledge informed me that my son incurs a hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and stoning is upon the wife of this one. I think he said: So judge between us by the Book of Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will surely judge between you by the Book of Allah. As for the sheep and the slave girl, they are returned to you; as for your son, he incurs a hundred lashes and banishment for a year."" And he said to a man of Aslam called Unays: ""Stand, O Unays, and question the wife of this one; if she confesses, stone her."""
"5196","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qanabi from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah from Abu Hurayra and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that they both informed him that two men disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said: O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah! The other, who was the more knowledgeable of the two, said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah, and permit me to speak, or permit me that I may speak! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Speak."" He said: My son was a hired laborer with this one, and a hired laborer is a hireling, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son incurred stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl of mine. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they informed me that my son incurs a hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and stoning is only upon his wife! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes indeed, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will surely judge between you by the Book of Allah. As for your sheep and your slave girl, they are returned to you."" And he lashed his son a hundred and banished him for a year, and ordered Unays al-Aslami to go to the wife of the other; if she confessed, he would stone her. So she confessed and he stoned her."
"5197","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam, who informed us from Malik, al-Layth, and Sufyan ibn Uyayna, some adding to others, from Ibn Shihab from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Masud from Abu Hurayra and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani. Sufyan and Shibl said: Two men disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said: O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah! The other, the more knowledgeable of them, said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah, and permit me to speak! He said: ""Speak."" He said: My son was a hired laborer with this one; he said: a hired laborer is a hireling; and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son incurred stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl of mine. Then I asked the people of knowledge and was informed that my son incurs only a hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and that stoning is upon his wife. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes indeed, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will surely judge between you by the Book of Allah. As for your slave girl and your sheep, they are returned to you."" And he lashed his son a hundred and banished him for a year, and ordered Unays al-Aslami to go to the wife of the other; if she confessed, he would stone her. So she confessed and he stoned her."
"5198","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Sufyan ibn Uyayna from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Abu Hurayra, Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, and Shibl, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5199","Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi from Abd Allah ibn Salih, who related to me from al-Layth from Ibn Shihab from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Abu Hurayra and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a Bedouin man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned similar to it."
"5200","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi from Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak from Ismail ibn Ayyash from Abu Wahb Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayd al-Kalai from Maruf from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say regarding one who has not married when he commits adultery: ""A hundred lashes and banishment for a year."""
"5201","Narrated Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri from Ahmad ibn Salih from Ibn Wahb who said: I heard Malik, Yunus ibn Yazid, and others, that Ibn Shihab informed them from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani and Abu Hurayra, that two men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disputing before him. One of them said: O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah! The other, the more knowledgeable of the two, said: Yes indeed, judge between us by the Book of Allah, and permit me to speak! He said: ""Speak."" He said: My son was a hired laborer with this one, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son incurred stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl of mine. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they informed me that my son incurs only a hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and stoning is only upon his wife. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes indeed, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will surely judge between you by the Book of Allah. As for your sheep and your slave girl, they are returned to you."" And he lashed his son a hundred and banished him for a year, and ordered Unays al-Aslami to stone the wife of the other if she confessed. So she confessed and he stoned her."
"5202","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Ubayd Allah ibn Sad from his uncle from his father from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ibn Shihab, that Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah informed him that Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani and Abu Hurayra informed him that two men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disputing before him. One of them said: O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah, and permit me to speak! He said: ""Speak."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, my son was a hired laborer with this one, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son incurred stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they informed me that my son incurs a hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and that stoning is upon his wife! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes indeed, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will surely judge between you by the Book of Allah. As for your sheep and your slave girl, they are returned to you."" He said: And he lashed his son a hundred and banished him for a year, and ordered Unays al-Aslami to stone the wife of the other, and he stoned her."
"5203","Narrated Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) command regarding one who commits adultery without having married: a hundred lashes and banishment for a year."
"5204","Narrated Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed regarding one who commits adultery without having married: a hundred lashes and banishment for a year."
"5205","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Usayd al-Asbahani from Yunus ibn Habib from Abu Dawud from Ibn Abi Dhib and Zamaa ibn Salih from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Zayd ibn Khalid and from Abu Hurayra who said: Two men disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said: I adjure you by Allah, judge between us only by the Book of Allah! His opponent stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son was a hired laborer with this one, meaning his hireling, and he committed adultery with his wife. So I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a servant. When I asked the people of knowledge, they informed me that my son incurs only a hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and that stoning is upon the wife of this one! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will surely judge between you by the Book of Allah. As for the hundred sheep and the servant, they are returned to you; your son incurs a hundred lashes and banishment for a year. Go, O Unays, to the wife of this one; if she confesses, stone her."" So he questioned her and she confessed, and he stoned her."
"5206","Narrated Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Anbar al-Basri and Muhammad ibn al-Rabi ibn Shahin, who said: Narrated Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi from Sulayman ibn Kathir from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that two men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said: I adjure you, O Messenger of Allah, judge between me and this one only by the Book of Allah, and permit me! He said: My son was a hired laborer with this one, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son incurred stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl. I asked the people of knowledge, and they informed me that my son incurs a hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and that stoning is upon the wife of this one! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will surely judge between you by the Book of Allah. As for the slave girl and the sheep, they are returned to you; your son incurs a hundred lashes and banishment for a year."" And he said: ""Go, O Unays, to the wife of this one; if she confesses, stone her."" So he went to her in the morning and she confessed, and he stoned her."
"5207","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Abu Hurayra and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a slave woman who has not married. He said: ""If she commits adultery, lash her; then if she commits adultery in the third or in the fourth,"" al-Zuhri doubted, ""then sell her even for a rope."""
"5208","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qanabi from Malik, and narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam, and narrated Bakr ibn Sahl from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, who said: Malik informed us from Ibn Shihab from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Masud from Abu Hurayra and from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a slave woman when she commits adultery without having married. He said: ""If she commits adultery, lash her; then if she commits adultery, lash her; then if she commits adultery, lash her, then sell her even for a rope."" Ibn Shihab said: ""And I do not know whether after the third or the fourth; and a dafir is a rope."""
"5209","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi, and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, who said: Narrated Sufyan ibn Uyayna from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah from Abu Hurayra, Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, and Shibl, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man asked him about a slave woman who commits adultery before marrying. He said: ""Lash her."" He said: Then if she commits adultery? He said: ""Lash her."" Then he said in the third or in the fourth: ""Sell her even for a dafir; and a dafir is a rope of hair."""
"5210","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib from Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar from Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim from al-Walid ibn Kathir from al-Zuhri, that Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba related to him that he heard Abu Hurayra and Zayd ibn Khalid, that they witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about a slave woman when she commits adultery. He said: ""Lash her three times, then sell her even for a halter."""
"5211","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Usayd al-Asbahani from Yunus ibn Habib from Abu Dawud from Zamaa ibn Salih from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani and from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the slave woman of one of you commits adultery, let him lash her; if she returns, let him lash her; if she returns, let him lash her; if she returns a fourth time, let him sell her even for a dafir of hair."""
"5212","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Ubayd Allah ibn Sad from his uncle from his father from Salih ibn Kaysan, that Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah informed him that Abu Hurayra and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani informed him that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about a slave woman who commits adultery without having married. He said: ""Lash her if she commits adultery, then if she commits adultery, lash her, then sell her even for a dafir,"" in the third or in the fourth."
"5213","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, who related to me from Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili from Abd Allah ibn Jafar from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the slave woman of one of you commits adultery, let him lash her; then if she commits adultery, let him lash her; then if she commits adultery, let him lash her; then if she commits adultery, let him sell her even for a dafir."""
"5214","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, who informed us from Abd al-Razzaq, who informed us from Mamar from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: A man cursed a rooster that crowed near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""Do not curse it, for it calls to prayer."""
"5215","Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Asim ibn Ali from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade reviling the rooster, and said: ""It gives the call to prayer."""
"5216","Narrated Said ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti from Amr ibn Awn, who informed us from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not revile the rooster, for it wakes for prayer."""
"5217","Narrated Said ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti from Amr ibn Awn, who informed us from Hafs ibn Sulayman from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Zayd ibn Khalid who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not revile the rooster, for it announces the time."""
"5218","Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, who informed us from Malik from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not revile the rooster."""
"5219","Narrated Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, who informed us from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer at al-Hudaybiya after rain in the night. When he finished he said: ""Have you not heard what your Lord said tonight? He said: Never have I bestowed a blessing upon My servants except that a group of them became disbelievers in it by morning. As for whoever praised Me for My rain and lauded Me, that one believes in Me and disbelieves in the star; as for whoever said: We were rained upon by such-and-such a lunar station, that is the one who believes in the star and disbelieves in My blessing."""
"5220","Narrated Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi from Abd Allah ibn Raja, who informed us from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Zayd ibn Khalid who said: We were rained upon with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Hudaybiya. When morning came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do you know what your Lord said?"" We said: Allah and His Messenger know best, he said it twice. Then he said: ""Among My servants, some have become believers and some disbelievers this morning. As for the one who says: We were rained upon by such-and-such a lunar station, that one is a disbeliever in Me, a believer in the star; as for the one who says: This is mercy, and this is the provision of Allah, that one is a believer in Me, a disbeliever in the star."""
"5221","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: We were given rain at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). In the morning he said: Do you know what your Lord said last night? He said: I did not bestow any blessing upon My servants but a party of them became disbelievers in it in the morning, saying: We were given rain by such-and-such star. As for whoever believed in Me and praised Me for giving drink, that is the one who believed in Me and disbelieved in the star. And as for whoever said: We were given rain by such-and-such star, that is the one who believed in the star and disbelieved in Me."
"5222","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same as it."
"5223","Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, from Umarah ibn Abd Allah ibn Tumah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sheep among his Companions. He gave me a young male goat, a jadhah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I sacrifice it, for it is a jadhah of goats? He said: Yes. So I sacrificed it."
"5224","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Umarah ibn Abd Allah ibn Tumah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sacrificial animals among his Companions. He gave me a young male goat and I found it to be a jadhah, so I returned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a jadhah. He said: Sacrifice it."
"5225","Muhammad ibn Fada al-Jawhari al-Basri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khalaf Abu Salamah al-Jubari narrated, Abd al-Ala narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Umarah ibn Abd Allah ibn Tumah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sheep among his Companions for sacrifices. He gave me a young male goat. I returned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a jadhah. He said: Sacrifice it. So I sacrificed it."
"5226","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Umarah ibn Abd Allah ibn Tumah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sacrifices among his Companions. He gave me a young male goat, a jadhah of goats. I brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: It is a jadhah. He said: Sacrifice it."
"5227","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd al-Ala narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution."
"5228","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution."
"5229","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Had it not been that I would impose hardship upon my nation, I would have commanded them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer."
"5230","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Yala ibn Ubayd narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl and Yala ibn Ubayd narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Zayd ibn Khalid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had it not been that I would impose hardship upon my nation, I would have commanded them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer. Zayd would place the tooth-stick with himself in the position of the pen at the ear of the scribe; whenever he stood for prayer he used the tooth-stick."
"5231","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated. And Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Durust narrated — both said: Abu Ismail al-Qannad narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has indeed taken part in battle, and whoever looks after a warrior among his family with good has indeed taken part in battle."
"5232","Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Daqqaq narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated, Ali ibn al-Mubarak informed, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior has indeed taken part in battle, and whoever looks after him with good has indeed taken part in battle."
"5233","Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated. And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muawiyah ibn Hisham and Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated — they said: Shayban narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has indeed taken part in battle, and whoever looks after a warrior among his family has indeed taken part in battle."
"5234","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us. And Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us — both said: Hisham ibn Khalid narrated, Uqbah ibn Alqamah narrated, al-Awzai narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Busr ibn Said, Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has indeed taken part in battle, and whoever looks after a warrior among his family has indeed taken part in battle."
"5235","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Harb ibn Shaddad narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior has indeed taken part in battle, and whoever looks after a warrior among his family with good has indeed taken part in battle."
"5236","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Muqad narrated, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abd al-Warith ibn Said and Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, both from Husayn al-Muallim, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has indeed taken part in battle, and whoever looks after a warrior among his family with good has indeed taken part in battle."
"5237","Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated. And Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated — both said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him that Busr ibn Said narrated to him, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has indeed taken part in battle, and whoever looks after him among his family with good has indeed taken part in battle."
"5238","Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated. And Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated — both from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever equips a warrior or looks after him among his family has indeed taken part in battle."
"5239","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, my father narrated to me. And Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated — both said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, Musa ibn Yaqub informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Shihab, from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Suraqah, from Busr ibn Said, that Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior, he has the like of his reward, and whoever looks after a warrior among his family, he has the like of his reward. Ibn Shihab said: Then Busr ibn Said informed me of it."
"5240","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah, he has the like of his reward, and whoever looks after a warrior in the path of Allah among his family with good and spends, he has the like of his reward."
"5241","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed, al-Thawri and Malik informed me, from Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Said, who said: Abu Juhaym al-Ansari sent me to Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani to ask him what he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man passing in front of one praying. He said: I heard him say: For one to stand in his place forty is better than passing in front of one praying. He said: I do not know whether he said forty years, or forty months, or forty days."
"5242","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated. And Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated — both said: Sufyan narrated, Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated, from Busr ibn Said, who said: Abu al-Juhaym, the nephew of Ubayy ibn Kab, sent me to Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani to ask him what he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say about one passing in front of one praying. I asked him and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For one of you to stand forty is better for him than passing in front of one praying; he does not know whether forty years, or forty months, or forty days."
"5243","Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about lost property. He said: Announce it for a year; if its owner comes, otherwise know its container and its tie and its number, then consume it; if its owner comes, return it to him."
"5244","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated, Abu al-Nadr narrated to me, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about lost property. He said: Announce it for a year; if it is recognized, deliver it, otherwise know its container and its number; if its owner comes, deliver it."
"5245","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated. And Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, Ghassan ibn al-Mufaddal al-Ghallabi narrated — both said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques, and let them go out unscented."
"5246","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah informed, he said: Khalid informed, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques, and let them go out unscented."
"5247","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, the two Egyptians, narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever receives a kindness from his brother without asking and without aspiring to it, let him accept it and not reject it, for it is provision that Allah has driven to him."
"5248","Ata ibn Yasar from Zayd ibn Khalid: Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then prays two units without becoming inattentive in them, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"5249","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same as it."
"5250","Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution and performs ablution well, then prays two units without becoming inattentive in them, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"5251","Abd Allah ibn Qays ibn Makhramah from Zayd ibn Khalid: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated, from Malik, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, that Abd Allah ibn Qays ibn Makhramah informed him, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that he said: I shall certainly observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tonight. So I lay my head on his threshold or his tent. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two light units, then prayed two long units, then prayed two units shorter than the two before them, then prayed two units shorter than the two before them, then prayed two units shorter than the two before them, then prayed witr; that is thirteen."
"5252","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Qays, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same as it."
"5253","Abu Salih al-Samman from Zayd ibn Khalid: Muttalib ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Said, from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Zayd ibn Khalid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, Ghifar, Muzaynah, and whoever is of Juhaynah and Ashja are my allies; they have no protector besides Allah and His Messenger."
"5254","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, my father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Said, from Yaqub ibn Khalid, from Abu Salih al-Samman — Yahya said: I know it only from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, Ghifar, and whoever is of Ashja and Juhaynah are allied adherents, my allies; they have no protector besides Allah and His Messenger."
"5255","Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, from Zayd ibn Khalid: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: A bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about lost property. He said: Announce it for a year, then know its container and its tie — or he said: its vessel — if its owner comes, hand it to him; otherwise spend it or enjoy it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, stray sheep? He said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. He said: He asked him about stray camels, and his face changed, and he said: What have you to do with it? With it are its shoes and its water-skin; it comes to water and eats trees; leave it until its owner finds it."
"5256","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated, from Malik, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about lost property. He said: Know its container and its tie, then announce it for a year; if its owner comes, otherwise it is yours to deal with. He said: Stray sheep? He said: For you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. He said: Stray camels? He said: What have you to do with it? With it are its water-skin and its shoes; it comes to water and eats trees until its owner finds it."
"5257","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated. And Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibn Aishah narrated — they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Yahya ibn Said and Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about stray camels. He said: What have you to do with it? With it are its water-skin and its shoes; it eats trees and comes to water until its seeker comes to it. Then he asked him about stray sheep and he said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. Then he asked him about lost property and he said: Know its container and its number; if its owner comes and recognizes it, hand it to him; otherwise it is yours."
"5258","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, inform me about lost property. He said: Know its container and its tie, then announce it for a year; if its seeker comes, return it to him; otherwise spend it. He said: Inform me about stray sheep? He said: Take it, for it is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. He said: Inform me about stray camels? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until his cheeks reddened, then said: What have you to do with it? With it are its shoes and its water-skin; it comes to water and eats trees; leave it until its owner finds it."
"5259","Hamid ibn Sadan ibn Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, that Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman informed him, from Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about stray sheep, and he said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. And he asked him about stray camels and he said: What have you to do with stray camels? With it are its water-skin and its shoes; it comes to water and eats trees; leave it until its owner finds it."
"5260","Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, from Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was with him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, lost property? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Announce it for a year; if no seeker comes for it, spend it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about stray sheep? He said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about stray camels? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until his face reddened, then said: What have you to do with it? With it are its shoes and its water-skin; it comes to water and eats trees until its owner finds it."
"5261","Hafs ibn Umar al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated, Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lost property, and he said: Announce it for a year, then know its tie, then spend it; if its owner comes, deliver it to him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, stray sheep? He said: Take it, for it is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. He said: O Messenger of Allah, stray camels? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until his cheeks reddened or his face reddened, then said: What have you to do with it? With it are its shoes and its water-skin until its owner finds it."
"5262","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Yahya ibn Said and Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about stray camels? He became angry and his cheeks reddened. He said: What have you to do with it? With it are shoes and water-skin; it eats from trees and drinks from water until its owner finds it. He said: Stray sheep? He said: For you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. He said: Lost property? He said: Know its container and its tie, then announce it; if it is not recognized, mix it with your property."
"5263","Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Rabiah, from Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same as it."
"5264","Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated, from Abbad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from his father Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about stray sheep. He said: For you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. And he was asked about stray camels; he became angry and his face reddened, and said: With it are its shoes and its water-skin; it comes to water and grazes trees. And he was asked about lost property and said: Announce it for a year; if its owner comes, hand it to him; otherwise know its tie or its container, then place it in your property; if its owner comes, you hand it to him."
"5265","Salih ibn Nabhan, freedman of al-Tawamah, from Zayd ibn Khalid: Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ali ibn Qutaybah al-Rifai narrated, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then leave until we reached the market, and he could still see the place where his arrow fell."
"5266","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, may Allah have mercy on him, Ibn al-Ashjai narrated, my father narrated to me, from Sufyan, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani say: I used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then go out to the market; if I were to shoot, I would still see the places where my arrows fell."
"5267","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, Abu Ayyub narrated to me, from Salih, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not go from one prayer to another without using the tooth-stick."
"5268","Abu Harb ibn Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani from his father: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Harun ibn Abd Allah narrated — both said: Qudamah ibn Muhammad al-Ashjai narrated, Makhramah ibn Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Harb ibn Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: I bear witness concerning my father Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to give glad tidings to the people that whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner to Him, then Paradise is his."
"5269","Khalid ibn Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani from his father: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Khalid ibn Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — with the hadith of lost property."
"5270","Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani from his father: Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated, Man ibn Isa narrated, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade snatching and plundering."
"5271","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated — both said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Ibn Abi Dhib informed, from a freedman of Juhaynah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Khalid, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade plundering and mutilation."
"5272","Ayyub ibn Khalid al-Ansari from Zayd ibn Khalid: al-Husayn ibn Ulayl al-Anazi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, from Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi, Ayyub ibn Khalid al-Ansari informed me, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: I and a companion of mine were on the day of Khaybar bargaining with a woman over temporary marriage concerning the term, and she bargaining with us, when someone came to us and informed us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had forbidden temporary marriage and had forbidden eating every beast of prey with fangs and domestic donkeys."
"5273","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani: Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides breakfast for a fasting person, he has the like of his reward without anything diminishing from his reward, and whoever equips a pilgrim, or equips a warrior, or looks after him among his family, he has the like of his reward without anything diminishing from his reward."
"5274","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim and Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides breakfast for a fasting person, or equips a warrior, or equips a pilgrim, he has the like of their rewards without anything diminishing from their rewards."
"5275","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides breakfast for a fasting person, feeding him and giving him drink, he has the like of his reward without anything diminishing from his reward."
"5276","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides breakfast for a fasting person, or enables a man to perform hajj, or equips a warrior, or looks after him among his family, he has the like of his reward."
"5277","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Abu Shihab narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior, or a pilgrim, or looks after him among his family, or provides breakfast for a fasting person, he has the like of his reward without that diminishing it."
"5278","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides breakfast for a fasting person, he has the like of the reward of the fasting person, and nothing diminishes from the reward of the fasting person, and whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah or looks after him among his family, he has the like of the reward of the warrior in that nothing diminishes from the warrior."
"5279","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibn Aishah and Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated — both said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides breakfast for a fasting person, the like of his reward is written for him in that nothing diminishes from the reward of the fasting person, and whoever equips a warrior or looks after him among his family, he has the like of his reward in that nothing diminishes from the reward of the warrior."
"5280","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Jarir and Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides breakfast for a fasting person, the like of his reward is written for him in that nothing diminishes from the reward of the fasting person, and whoever equips a warrior or looks after him among his family, he has the like of his reward in that nothing diminishes from the reward of the warrior."
"5281","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated, Maqil ibn Ubayd Allah narrated, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah and Ikrimah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides breakfast for a fasting person, he has the like of his reward and nothing diminishes from his reward, and whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah, he has the like of his reward and nothing diminishes from his reward."
"5282","Bishr ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, both said: Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated, Umar ibn Qays narrated, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah or looks after him among his family with good, he has the like of the reward of the warrior without anything diminishing from his reward, and whoever provides breakfast for a fasting person, he has the like of his reward."
"5283","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides breakfast for a fasting person, or equips a pilgrim or a warrior, he has the like of their rewards without anything diminishing from their rewards."
"5284","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray in your houses and do not take them as graves."
"5285","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Pray in your houses and do not take them as graves."
"5286","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Jarir and Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take your houses as graves, and pray in them."
"5287","Abu Salim al-Jayshani from Zayd ibn Khalid: Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to him, from Abu Salim al-Jayshani, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shelters a stray animal is astray unless he announces it."
"5288","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Harun ibn Maruf narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Abu Salim al-Jayshani, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the same as it."
"5289","Zayd ibn Kab al-Sulami, then al-Bahzi: Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Yahya ibn Said informed, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Isa ibn Talhah, from Umayr ibn Salamah al-Damri, from al-Bahzi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left intending Makkah until, when he was at part of Wadi al-Rawha, the people found a hamstrung wild donkey. They mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Leave it until its owner comes. Al-Bahzi came — and he was its owner — and said: O Messenger of Allah, you may have this donkey. He commanded Abu Bakr to distribute it among the companies while they were in pilgrim sanctity. Then we passed until, when we were at al-Uthayah, there was a gazelle standing in shade with an arrow in it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a man to stand by it until he informed the people about it."
"5290","Zayd ibn al-Dathinah al-Ansari, then of Banu Bayadah: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, who said: Part of the account of Khubayb ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, then of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and Asim ibn Thabit ibn al-Aflah ibn Amr ibn Awf, and Zayd ibn al-Dathinah al-Ansari of Banu Bayadah, is that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them as scouts toward Makkah to inform him of the news of Quraysh. They traveled by the Najd road until, when they were at al-Raji of Najd, Banu Lihyan of Hudhayl intercepted them. As for Asim ibn Thabit, he fought with his sword until he was killed. As for Khubayb and Zayd ibn al-Dathinah, they ascended the mountain and the people could not overcome them until they gave them covenants and pledges; they came down to them, and they bound them with bonds, then brought them to Makkah and sold them to Quraysh. As for Khubayb, Utbah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, brother of Husayn ibn al-Harith, bought him, and Abu Ihab ibn Aziz ibn Qays ibn Suwayd ibn Rabiah ibn Adas ibn Abd Allah ibn Darim shared with him in buying him, and Qays ibn Suwayd ibn Rabiah was the maternal brother of Amir ibn Nawfal, their mother the daughter of Nahshal al-Tamimiyyah, and Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, al-Akhnas ibn Sharnun ibn Ilaj ibn Ghubrah al-Thaqafi, Ubaydah ibn Hakim al-Sulami then al-Dhakwani, Umayyah ibn Utbah ibn Hammam ibn Hanzalah of Banu Darim and Banu al-Hadrami, Saiyah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Qays of Banu Amir ibn Luayy, and Safwan ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf ibn Wahb al-Jumahi — they handed him to Utbah ibn al-Harith, who imprisoned him in a house. He stayed with him as long as Allah willed. A woman of the family of Utbah ibn al-Harith ibn Amir would release him and feed him. He said to her: When the people intend to kill me, inform me before that. When they intended to kill him, she informed him. He said to her: Seek for me an iron blade to clean myself with — meaning to shave his pubic hair. The son of the woman who was attending to him entered with the razor in his hand; he took the boy by the hand and said: Has Allah given you power over us? She said: This is not my opinion of you. Then he handed her the razor and said: I was only joking. The people who had shared in him took him out, and the people of Makkah went out with them, with a wooden cross, until when they were at al-Tanim they set up that wood and crucified him upon it. The one who carried out his killing was Utbah ibn al-Harith; Abu Husayn was small and was with the people. They killed him for al-Harith ibn Amir, who had been killed on the day of Badr as a disbeliever. Khubayb said to them at his killing: Release me from the bonds until I pray two units — they released him, and he prayed two light units, then turned and said: Were it not that you would think I am afraid of death, I would have lengthened them; therefore I shortened them. He said: O Allah, I see only the face of an enemy; O Allah, I find no messenger to Your Messenger, so convey my greeting to him. Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of that. Khubayb said as they raised him upon the wood: O Allah, count them in number, kill them separately, and leave none of them. The sons of the polytheists who had been killed on the day of Badr killed Khubayb ibn Adi. When they put weapons into him while crucified, they called to him and adjured him: Would you love Muhammad in your place? He said: No, by the great Allah, I would not love that even a thorn prick his foot as ransom for me. They laughed. Khubayb said when they raised him upon the wood — the confederates, the confederates — a cut-off limb. As for Zayd ibn al-Dithinnah, Safwan ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf bought him and killed him for his father Umayyah ibn Khalaf; Nistas, freedman of Banu Jumah, killed him. Both were killed at al-Tanim. Amr ibn Umayyah buried Khubayb. Hassan ibn Thabit said concerning Khubayb: verses ending at the edge ..."
"5291","Those named Ziyad; Ziyad ibn al-Harith al-Sudai, who would reside in Egypt: Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum narrated, from Ziyad ibn Nuaym, from Ziyad ibn al-Harith al-Sudai, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him. It reached me that he intended to send an army to my people, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, hold back the army, and I guarantee you their Islam and obedience. He said: Do so. He wrote to them, and a delegation of them came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with their Islam and obedience. He said: O brother of Suda, you are obeyed among your people. I said: Rather Allah guided them and did good to them. He said: Shall I not appoint you over them? I said: Yes. He appointed me over them and wrote for me a document to that effect, and I asked him from their charities and he did so. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was then on one of his journeys; he alighted at a stop and we rested early in the night. I stayed with him while his companions kept separating until none of them remained with him but me. When dawn approached, he commanded me and I called the adhan, then said to me: O brother of Suda, do you have water? I said: Yes, a little, not enough for you. He said: Pour it into the vessel, then bring it to me. I brought it to him and he put his hand into it, and I saw between every two fingers of his fingers a spring gushing. He said: O brother of Suda, were it not that I feel shy before my Lord, we would have given drink and sought drink. Call among the people: Whoever wants ablution. Whoever scooped, scooped, and Bilal came to make the iqamah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The brother of Suda called the adhan, and whoever calls the adhan, he makes the iqamah. When he prayed Fajr, the people of the stop came complaining about their agent and saying: O Messenger of Allah, inform us of what was between us and our people in the pre-Islamic time. He turned to his companions, and I among them, and said: There is no good in leadership for a believing man. It fell into my mind. A beggar came and asked him, and he said: Whoever asks people out of sufficiency, it is headache in the head and ailment in the belly. He said: Give me from the charities. He said: Allah was not pleased in charities with the judgment of a prophet or other than him until He made them eight shares; if you are of them, I give you your right. In the morning I said: O Messenger of Allah, accept your appointment; I have no need of it. He said: Why? I said: I heard you say: There is no good in leadership for a believing man, and I have believed, and I heard you say: Whoever asks people out of sufficiency, it is headache in the head and ailment in the belly, and I asked you while rich. He said: It is that; if you wish, take, and if you wish, leave. I said: Rather I leave. He said: Point me to a man I may appoint. I pointed him to a man of the delegation and he appointed him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we have a well whose water suffices us and we gather at it in winter, and in summer it lessens and we disperse to waters around us, and today we cannot disperse; all around us are enemies. Supplicate Allah to make its water ample for us. He called for seven pebbles and held them in his palm, then said: Go and cast them one by one, mentioning the name of Allah. They could no longer see its bottom after that."
"5292","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Ziyad ibn Nuaym, from Ziyad ibn al-Harith al-Sudai, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he commanded me and I called the adhan for Fajr. Bilal came to make the iqamah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bilal, the brother of Suda called the adhan, and whoever calls the adhan, he makes the iqamah."
"5293","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Ziyad ibn Nuaym, from Ziyad ibn al-Harith al-Sudai, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; the morning prayer came, and he said to me: Call the adhan, O brother of Suda. I called the adhan while on my mount."
"5294","Ziyad ibn Labid al-Ansari, Badri, Aqabi, who would reside in Kufah, kunyah Abu Abd Allah: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then of Banu Bayadah ibn Amir ibn Zurayq ibn Abd ibn Harithah: Ziyad ibn Labid ibn Thalabah ibn Sinan ibn Amir ibn Adi ibn Umayyah."
"5295","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed al-Aqabah, then of Banu Bayadah: Ziyad ibn Labid, and he witnessed Badr."
"5296","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated. And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated — both said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated, al-Amash narrated, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Ziyad ibn Labid al-Ansari, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was speaking to his companions, saying: How, when the time of knowledge has gone. I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, how does the time of knowledge go while we recite the Quran and teach it to our sons, and our sons will teach it to their sons until the Hour comes? He said: May your mother be bereaved of you, O son of Labid, I used to consider you among the most understanding of the people of Madinah. Do not the Jews and Christians read the Torah and the Gospel yet benefit nothing from them?"
"5297","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Waki narrated, al-Amash narrated, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Ziyad ibn Labid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned something and said: That is at the time of the going of knowledge. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how does knowledge go while we recite the Quran and teach it to our sons, and our sons will teach it to their sons until the Day of Resurrection? He said: May your mother be bereaved of you, Ziyad, I used to consider you among the most understanding men of Madinah. Do not these Jews and Christians read the Torah and the Gospel yet act upon nothing of them?"
"5298","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Salim narrating from Ibn Labid al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the time of the going of knowledge. I said: How, when among us is the Book of Allah; we teach it to our sons and our sons will teach it to their sons? He said: May your mother be bereaved of you, son of Labid, I did not think you but among the most intelligent of the people of Madinah. Are not the Jews and Christians with the Book of Allah, the Torah and the Gospel, yet they benefited nothing from it?"
"5299","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed, from Abu Tuwalah, from Ziyad ibn Labid al-Ansari, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how is knowledge taken while we recite the Quran and teach it to our sons, our women, and our slaves? He said: By Allah, I used to think you, O Ziyad, among the jurists of the Muslims. Do you not know that the Torah and the Gospel were sent down to the Jews and Christians, yet they did not benefit when they did not act upon them?"
"5300","Ziyad Abu al-Agharr al-Nahshali, who would reside in Basrah: al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-Askari narrated to us, both said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated, Abu al-Haytham al-Qassab narrated, Ghassan ibn al-Agharr al-Nahshali narrated, my father narrated to me, from his father, that he came with a camel of his to Madinah loaded with food. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him and said: O bedouin, what are you carrying? I said: I am preparing wheat. He said to me: What do you want? I said: I want to sell it. He wiped my head and said: Treat the bedouin well in bargaining."
"5301","Ziyad ibn Amr al-Juhani, ally of the Ansar, then of Banu Saidah, Badri: al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr of the Ansar, then of Banu Saidah ibn Kab ibn al-Khazraj: Ziyad ibn Amr al-Juhani, an ally of theirs."
"5302","Ziyad ibn al-Fard: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Firdaws ibn al-Ashari narrated, Masud ibn Sulayman narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab, from Abu al-Yasar ibn Amr and Ziyad ibn al-Fard, that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to Ammar: The transgressing party will kill you."
"5303","Ziyad ibn Jahwar al-Lakhmi, who would reside in Syria: Hudhafi ibn Humayd ibn al-Mustanir ibn al-Musawir ibn Hudhafi ibn Amir ibn Iyad ibn Muhraq al-Ammi al-Lakhmi narrated to us, my father Humayd ibn al-Mustanir narrated to me, from his maternal uncle, brother of his mother, Khalid ibn Musa, my father narrated to me, from his grandfather Ziyad ibn Jahwar, who said: A letter from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, in it: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; from Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, to Ziyad ibn Jahwar: You are safe; I praise to you Allah besides whom there is no god. To proceed, I remind you of Allah and the Last Day. To proceed, every religion that people profess shall be laid down except Islam; know that."
"5304","Zubayb ibn Thalabah al-Anbari, who would reside in Basrah: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated, Shuayth ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Zubayb ibn Thalabah narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever owes a slave of the children of Ismail, let him free one of Bal-anbar."
"5305","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated, Shuayth ibn Abd Allah ibn Zubayb narrated. And Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Sad ibn Ammar ibn Shuayth ibn Thalabah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Zubayb ibn Thalabah al-Anbari narrated, my father Ammar narrated to me, my grandfather Shuayth narrated to me, Ubayd Allah ibn Zubayb ibn Thalabah al-Anbari narrated to me that his father Zubayb ibn Thalabah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent his companions and they took captives of Banu al-Anbar while they were mukhadramun and had become Muslim. Zubayb mounted a she-camel of his, then came before the people. He said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, your companions took captives of Banu al-Anbar while they are mukhadramun and have become Muslim. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have proof, O Zubayb? He said: Yes. Samurah ibn Amr testified and Zubayb swore. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return to Banu al-Anbar all that is theirs. They returned to them all but the thick blanket of my mother — Sad said: al-zirbiyyah is the velvet cloak — Zubayb came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, all that is theirs was returned to Banu al-Anbar except the thick blanket of my mother. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you know who took it? He said: Yes. He said: When the people attend prayer, sit at the door of the mosque; when you see your man, cling to him until he leaves prayer, then seek judgment between you and him. He did so. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished prayer, he turned to him and said: O Zubayb, O brother of Banu al-Anbar, what do you want with your captive? Zubayb burst into tears and released the man. He said: We intend good, Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: Is the thick blanket of the mother of Zubayb with you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, it has left my hand. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Take off your sword for him and add to him measures of food. He did so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew near Zubayb and wiped his hand over his head until he passed it to his navel. Zubayb said: Until I felt the coolness of the palm of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon my navel. Then he said: O Allah, grant him pardon and well-being. Then Zubayb left with the sword and sold it for two young she-camels of the charity of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they multiplied with Zubayb until they reached a hundred and more."
"5306","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated, Ammar ibn Shuayth narrated — with his chain, the same as it."
"5307","Zinba Abu Rawh al-Judhami, who would reside in Syria: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar and Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, and from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that Zinba Abu Rawh found a slave-boy of his with his slave-girl, so he cut his penis and cut his nose. The slave came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What carried you to what you did? He said: He did such-and-such. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the slave: Go, for you are free."
"5308","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym informed. And al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated — both said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah, from Salamah ibn Rawh ibn Zinba, that his grandfather castrated a slave of his; he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who freed him for the mutilation."
"5309","Those named Zuhayr; Zuhayr ibn Surad al-Jushami, who would reside in Syria: Ubayd Allah ibn Ramahi al-Jushami narrated to us, Abu Amr Ziyad ibn Tariq narrated — and he had lived a hundred and twenty years — he said: I heard Abu Jarwal Zuhayr ibn Surad al-Jushami say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took us captive on the day of Hunayn, the day of Hawazin, and began to distribute the youths and captives, I recited to him this verse: ... When he heard this verse he said: What was mine and Banu Abd al-Muttalib is yours. Quraysh said: What was ours is for Allah and His Messenger. The Ansar said: What was ours is for Allah and His Messenger."
"5310","Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the delegation of Hawazin, when they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Jiranah having become Muslim, said: We are root and kin, and we have suffered of affliction what is not hidden from you; bestow upon us, may Allah bestow upon you. A man of Hawazin, then of Banu Sad ibn Bakr, called Zuhayr, kunyah Abu Surad, stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, our women are your paternal and maternal aunts and your foster-mothers who raised you; had we attached ourselves to al-Harith ibn Abi Shimr and al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir, then there befell us from him what befell us from you, we would hope for his sympathy and kindness to us, and you are the best of those raised. Then he recited to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a verse he had composed, mentioning their kinship and what they had raised of him, and he said: ... The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are your sons and women dearer to you, or your properties? They said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave us choice between our properties and our women; rather return to us our properties and our women. He said: As for what was mine and Banu Abd al-Muttalib, it is yours; when I pray Zuhr with the people, stand and say: We seek intercession of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the Muslims, and of the Muslims with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning our sons and women; I shall give you at that and ask for you. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr with the people, they stood and spoke to him with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had commanded them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for what was mine and Banu Abd al-Muttalib, it is yours. The Emigrants said: What was ours is for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Ansar said the same. Al-Aqra ibn Habis said: As for me, O Messenger of Allah, and Banu Tamim, no. Uyaynah said the same. Abbas ibn Mirdas said: As for me and Banu Sulaym, no. Banu Sulaym said: As for what was ours, it is for the Messenger of Allah. Abbas said to Banu Sulaym: You weakened me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you holds to his right of these captives, he has six young she-camels of the first booty we obtain. They returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) their sons and women."
"5311","Zuhayr ibn Amr al-Hilali, who would reside in Basrah: Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated. And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated — both said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Qabisah ibn Mukhariq al-Hilali and Zuhayr ibn Amr, both said: When this verse came down upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And warn your nearest kin, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to a pile of stones of a mountain and ascended the highest stone, then said: O sons of Abd Manaf, I am a warner to you; my likeness and yours is but as a man who saw the enemy and went to warn his family, fearing they would precede him to his family, so he began to cry: O morning calamity, O morning calamity, you are attacked, you are attacked."
"5312","Zuhayr ibn Uthman al-Thaqafi: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated, my father narrated, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated, from Qatadah, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman al-Thaqafi, from a one-eyed man of Thaqif — Qatadah said: It was said he was called Maruf; if his name was not Zuhayr ibn Uthman, I do not know what his name was — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wedding feast on the first day is a right, the second is kindness, and the third is show and ostentation."
"5313","Zuhayr ibn Alqamah al-Thaqafi, who would reside in Kufah, and it is said: al-Bajali: Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated. And Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated. And al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jafar ibn Humayd narrated — they said: Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated, Iyad narrated, from Zuhayr ibn Alqamah, who said: A woman of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a son of hers who died, and the people seemed to rebuke her. She said: O Messenger of Allah, two have died for me since I entered Islam besides this one. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, you have been strongly protected from the Fire."
"5314","Zuhayr ibn Abi Alqamah al-Dubai, who would reside in Kufah: Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Aslam al-Minqari, from Zuhayr ibn Abi Alqamah al-Dubai, who said: A man of poor appearance came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Do you have wealth? He said: Yes, of every kind of wealth. He said: Let it be seen upon you, for Allah, mighty and majestic, loves to see the trace of His blessing upon His servant well, and does not love wretchedness and feigning wretchedness."
"5315","Zuhayr ibn Umayyah al-Hashimi: al-Hasan ibn Ulayl al-Anazi and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both said: Abu Kurayb narrated, Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated, Israil narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from al-Saib, who said: Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and Zuhayr ibn Umayyah came and sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they praised me to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know him better than you; he was my partner in the pre-Islamic time."
"5316","Those named Zahir; Zahir ibn Haram al-Ashjai, who would reside in Kufah: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Shadh ibn al-Fayyad narrated, Rafi ibn Salamah narrated, who said: I heard my father narrate from Salim, from a man of Ashja called Zahir ibn Haram al-Ashjai, who said: He was a bedouin man who would not come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came to him but with a rarity or gift he gifted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him in the market selling goods, and he had not come to him, so he embraced him from behind with his palms. He turned and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and kissed his palms. He said: Who will buy the slave? He said: Then you will find me, O Messenger of Allah, unsold. He said: But with Allah you are profitable."
"5317","Zahir ibn al-Aswad Abu Majzaah al-Aslami, who would reside in Kufah: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Majzaah ibn Zahir, from his father — and his father was of those who witnessed the Tree — who said: I was kindling under the pots — or he said: away from the pots — with donkey meats, when the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: Allah forbids you donkey meats."
"5318","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ismah ibn Sulayman al-Khazzaz narrated. And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated — both said: Sharik narrated, from Majzaah ibn Zahir, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded fasting Ashura and said: Whoever is fasting, let him complete his fast, and whoever was not fasting, let him complete the rest of his day."
"5319","Zari the Abdi, who would reside in Basrah: Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated, Matar ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Anaq narrated, from Umm Aban bint al-Wazi ibn Zari, from her grandfather al-Zari — and he was in the delegation of Abd al-Qays — who said: When we came to Madinah, we hastened down from our mounts and kissed the hands of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his feet. Al-Mundhir al-Ashajj waited until he went to his bag, put on his garment, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: In you are two traits Allah loves: forbearance and deliberation. He said: O Messenger of Allah, do I affect them, or did Allah fashion me upon them? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Rather Allah fashioned you upon them. Al-Mundhir said: Praise be to Allah who fashioned me upon two traits Allah and His Messenger love. It is said: The name of al-Ashajj is Aidh ibn Amr; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi mentioned it from Matar ibn Abd al-Rahman with this chain."
"5320","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated, Matar ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Anaq narrated, Umm Aban bint al-Wazi narrated to me, from her father, that her grandfather al-Zari went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); with him went a mad son of his, or a son of his sister. My grandfather said: When we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah, I said: O Messenger of Allah, with me is a mad son of mine, or son of my sister; I brought him to you for you to supplicate Allah, mighty and majestic, for him. He said: Bring him to me. I took him to him while he was in the saddle; I released him, cast off travel clothes from him, dressed him in two fine garments, and took his hand until I reached with him the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Bring him near me; place his back toward me. He took the gathered cloth of his garment from its top and bottom and began to strike his back until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, saying: Come out, enemy of Allah, come out, enemy of Allah. He began to look the look of a sound man, not his former look. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated him before him, called for water for him, wiped his face, and supplicated for him. There was none in the delegation after the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) better than him."
"5321","Zurarah ibn Juzayy: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shuaythi narrated, from Zufar ibn Wathimah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that Zurarah ibn Juzayy said to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan to give the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi inheritance from the blood-money of her husband."
"5322","Zurarah, an unattributed man: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated, Qurrah ibn Habib narrated, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, from Said ibn Amr ibn Jadah al-Makhzumi, from Ibn Zurarah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Taste the touch of Saqar; indeed We created everything with measure. He said: It was revealed about people of my nation at the end of time who deny the decree of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"5323","Zibriqan ibn Badr, who would reside near Madinah; what Zibriqan ibn Badr transmitted: Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated, Sahl ibn Waqqas al-Araji narrated, Jarwah ibn Jurthumah al-Araji narrated to me, Kahdal ibn Waqqas narrated to me, my father Waqqas ibn Sari narrated to me that his father Sari ibn al-Hakam narrated to him, who said: Zibriqan ibn Badr narrated to me that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned something. Zibriqan said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we make known? He said: No, O Zibriqan; hear for Allah and His Messenger and obey. He said: Hearing and obedience for Allah and His Messenger."
"5324","Chapter of Sin; Sad ibn Muadh al-Ansari, then al-Ashhali, Badri, Uhudi, kunyah Abu Amr, martyred on the day of the Trench: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr of the Ansar: Sad ibn Muadh ibn al-Numan ibn Imri al-Qays ibn Zayd ibn Abd al-Ashhal."
"5325","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr of the Ansar of al-Nabit, then of Banu Abd al-Ashhal: Sad ibn Muadh ibn al-Numan ibn Imri al-Qays."
"5326","Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakkai narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr of the Ansar, then of Banu Abd al-Ashhal: Sad ibn Muadh ibn al-Numan ibn Imri al-Qays ibn Zayd ibn Abd al-Ashhal ibn Jusham ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj ibn Amr ibn Awf ibn Malik ibn al-Aws."
"5327","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Asad al-Bajali narrated, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Awf, from al-Majishun, who said: Sad ibn Muadh said: Three things — apart from them I am weak: I never heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but I knew it is truth; I never prayed a prayer and told myself of other than it until I finished it; I never followed a funeral and told myself of other than what it says and is said to it."
"5328","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Layth ibn Harun al-Ukli narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, that Sad ibn Muadh said: Three traits are in me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never spoke a hadith but I believed it and knew it is truth; I never attended a dead but I made myself attend to what he says and what is said to him; I never prayed a prayer and told myself of other than it until I finished my prayer."
"5329","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated. And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, both said: Shubah narrated, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from Sad, father of Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Sad ibn Muadh concerning Banu Qurayzah. Sad came upon a donkey, his feet almost reaching the ground. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, he said to his companions: Stand to your chief. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: These have accepted your judgment; judge concerning them. He said: I judge concerning them that their fighters be killed and their offspring taken captive. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You judged with the judgment of Allah and the judgment of the King."
"5330","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri al-Dimashqi narrated, Sadaqah ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Iyad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sad ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Sad ibn Muadh came. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is your chief."
"5331","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: Sad ibn Muadh was struck in his elbow vein on the day of the Trench. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pitched for him a tent in the mosque to visit him near. He healed until his wound hardened for recovery. He said: O Allah, You know that the dearest people to me to fight are a people who denied Your Prophet, expelled him, fought him, and did; I think You have laid down war between us and them. O Allah, if You kept fighting between us and them, keep me to fight them. While he was one night, his wound burst and blood flowed from his wound until it entered a tent beside him. The people of the tent said: O people of the tent, what is this coming to us from your side? They looked, and Sad had burst his wound, blood gushing; he died."
"5332","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated, Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Amiri narrated, Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah narrated, from al-Hasan and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Sad ibn Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, was struck on the day of Qurayzah and al-Nadir; his elbow vein was cut. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized him; it festered and burst. He cauterized him a second time. Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Allah, do not take my soul until You delight my eye from Qurayzah and al-Nadir."
"5333","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, that Sad ibn Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, was struck on the day of the Trench with an arrow; it cut the elbow vein of his upper arm. They claim Hibban ibn Qays, of Banu Amir ibn Luayy, then brother of Banu al-Irqah, shot him; others say Abu Usamah al-Jushami shot him. Sad ibn Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Lord, heal me from Banu Qurayzah before death. The wound closed after it had burst. He said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained upon Banu Qurayzah until they asked him to place between him and them an arbitrator to come down upon his judgment. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Choose of my companions whom you wish; we shall listen to his word. They chose Sad ibn Muadh. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pleased with him, and they surrendered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded their weapons placed in a house; he commanded them bound and tied, placed in the house of Usamah ibn Zayd. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Sad ibn Muadh; he came upon a bedouin donkey, they claim the padding of its saddle of fiber. A man of Banu Abd al-Ashhal followed him, walking with him, magnifying the right of Banu Qurayzah, mentioning their alliance and what they did on the day of Buath, that they chose you over others hoping your sympathy and tenderness to them; spare them, for they are your beauty and number. The man repeated that much, and Sad did not return anything to him, until they drew near. The man said to him: Will you not return something to me? Sad said: By Allah, I do not care in Allah the blame of a blamer. The man left him and went to his people, despairing of his sparing them, and informed them of what he said to him and what he returned. Sad proceeded until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: O Sad, judge between us and them. Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I judge concerning them that their fighters be killed, their captives taken as booty, their properties taken, and their offspring and women taken captive. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sad ibn Muadh judged concerning them with the judgment of Allah. Some people claim they came down upon the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned judgment concerning them to Sad ibn Muadh. They were brought out group by group and their necks struck. Huyayy ibn Akhtab was brought out; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Has Allah disgraced you? He said: You overcame me, and I do not blame myself concerning you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded concerning him; he was brought to the oil stones at the market and his neck struck, all in the sight of Sad ibn Muadh. They claim the wound of Sad healed and hardened with recovery. Then he supplicated: O Allah, Lord of the heavens and earth, there was no people on earth more hateful to me than a people who denied Your Messenger and expelled him; I think You have laid down war between us and them. If fighting remains between us and them, keep me to fight them for You; if You laid down war between us and them, cause this place to burst and make my death in it. Allah, blessed and exalted, burst it while he lay in the middle of the night; they knew not of him until he died, and the wound did not close until he died, may Allah have mercy on him."
"5334","Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated, Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated, from Muslim ibn Abi Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The mother of Sad kept saying: Woe to the mother of Sad, Sad, firm and serious. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do not add to this; by Allah, as far as I knew, he was firm in his affair, strong in the affair of Allah."
"5335","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Umm Sad said when his bier was carried, weeping for him: Woe to the mother of Sad, Sad, firm, serious, a chief by whom a gap was filled. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every weeping woman lies except the weeper of Sad ibn Muadh."
"5336","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from his father, from his grandfather Alqamah, from Aishah, who said: When Sad ibn Muadh died, Abu Bakr wept and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, wept, until the weeping of Abu Bakr was known from the weeping of Umar, and the weeping of Umar from the weeping of Abu Bakr. I said to Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weep? She said: No, but he would grasp his beard, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"5337","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Muammal ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi narrated, Sahl Abu Hariz, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the funeral of Sad ibn Muadh, his tears running upon his beard, his hand in his beard."
"5338","Chapter: the Throne shook for the death of Sad ibn Muadh: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from his father, from his grandfather Alqamah ibn Waqqas, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to Dhu al-Hulayfah, the boys of the Ansar would meet him informing him about their families. It was said to Usayd ibn Hudayr: Your wife died. He wept. I was between him and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: Do you weep while you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the precedences you have? He said: I have right not to weep, when I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The woods of the Throne shook for the death of Sad ibn Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him."
"5339","Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Rahawayh, narrated, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated, Ibn Idris narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the one for whom the Throne moved, the doors of heaven opened, and seventy thousand angels witnessed him; he was squeezed a squeezing, then relieved from him."
"5340","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated, Awf narrated, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Throne shook for the death of Sad."
"5341","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for the death of Sad ibn Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him."
"5342","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the funeral of Sad ibn Muadh before them: The Throne of the Most Merciful, exalted, shook for it."
"5343","Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the funeral of Sad ibn Muadh before him, say: The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for it."
"5344","Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Zayd ibn Bishr al-Hadrami narrated, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated, from Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman, Ibn Lahiah, and Abu Amr al-Tujibi, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the funeral of Sad ibn Muadh before them: The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for it."
"5345","Ahmad ibn Abi Yahya al-Misri narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Waqqar narrated, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to me, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the funeral of Sad before him, say: The Throne of the Most Merciful, mighty and majestic, shook for it."
"5346","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated, Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd ibn Usamah al-Laythi narrated to me, from Muadh ibn Rifah, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of Sad ibn Muadh on the day he died while being buried: This righteous servant for whom the Throne of the Most Merciful moved, the doors of heaven opened, was pressed, then Allah relieved him."
"5347","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Amr ibn Malik al-Anbari narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, al-Awzai narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Muayqib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Throne shook for the death of Sad ibn Muadh."
"5348","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Thalabah ibn Sawa narrated, my uncle Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated, Said narrated, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, with the funeral of Sad laid down: The Throne shook for the death of Sad."
"5349","Abd Allah ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated, Umar ibn Sahl al-Mazini narrated, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated, from al-Hasan, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for the death of Sad."
"5350","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from a woman of the Ansar called Asma bint Yazid ibn Sakan, who said: When the funeral of Sad was brought out, his mother cried out. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Will your tear not cease and your grief go, for your son is the first for whom Allah smiled and the Throne shook for him."
"5351","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed, Mamar informed, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When the funeral of Sad ibn Muadh was carried, the hypocrites said: How light its funeral, for his judgment concerning Qurayzah. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No, but the angels carry him."
"5352","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muadh ibn Rifah narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: When Sad ibn Muadh was buried, while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he glorified Allah, and the people glorified with him long; then he magnified, and the people magnified with him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, for what did you glorify? He said: The grave pressed upon this righteous man until Allah relieved him by His mercy."
"5353","Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated, Abd Allah ibn Salim narrated, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: A suit of brocade was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); people began to feel it with their hands and marvel at it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does this please you? By Allah, the handkerchiefs of Sad in Paradise are better than it."
"5354","Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah informed, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a silk garment; they marveled at its softness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A handkerchief — or: some handkerchiefs — of Sad in Paradise is softer than it, or: better than it."
"5355","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: The Trench was in Shawwal, year five, and in it Sad ibn Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, died."
"5356","What Sad ibn Muadh transmitted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, Israil informed, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, who said: Sad ibn Muadh went for umrah and stayed with Abu Safwan Umayyah ibn Khalaf — and Umayyah, when he went to Syria passing Madinah, would stay with Sad. Umayyah said to Sad: Wait until midday when people are heedless, then go and circumambulate. While Sad circumambulated the Kabah secure, Abu Jahl came to him and said: Who is this circumambulating the Kabah secure? Sad said: I am Sad. Abu Jahl said: You circumambulate the House secure, while you sheltered Muhammad and his companions? There was between them until Umayyah said to Sad: Do not raise your voice upon Abu al-Hakam, for he is the chief of the valley people. Sad said to him: By Allah, if you prevent me from circumambulating the House, I shall cut off your trade to Syria. Umayyah kept saying to Sad: Do not raise your voice upon Abu al-Hakam, holding him. Sad became angry and said: Leave us from you, for I heard Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) claim he will kill you. He said: Me? He said: Yes. He said: By Allah, Muhammad does not lie. When they left, he returned to his wife and said: Do you know what my Yathribi brother said? He informed her. The wife of Umayyah said: Muhammad does not leave us. When the war-cry came and they went to Badr, she said to him: Do you not remember what your Yathribi brother said to you? He wanted not to go. Abu Jahl said: You are of the nobles of the valley people; travel with us a day or two. He traveled with them and Allah killed him."
"5357","Sad ibn Ubadah al-Ansari, then al-Khazraji, Aqabi, Badri, Uhudi, naqib, kunyah Abu Thabit, resided in Syria and died there: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr say: Sad ibn Ubadah is kunyah Abu Thabit."
"5358","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, concerning the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqabah of the Ansar, then of Banu Saidah ibn Kab ibn al-Khazraj: Sad ibn Ubadah ibn Dulaym ibn Harithah ibn Khuzaymah, and he is naqib, and he witnessed Badr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"5359","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqabah of the Ansar, then of Banu Saidah ibn Kab: Sad ibn Ubadah, and he is naqib."
"5360","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik narrated to me, from his brother Abd Allah, from his father Kab ibn Malik, who said: We went to the hajj in which we pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Aqabah; the naqib of Banu Saidah was Sad ibn Ubadah, and al-Mundhir ibn Amr."
"5361","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated, Ibrahim ibn al-Zibriqan informed, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr was with Ali ibn Abi Talib, and the banner of the Ansar was with Sad ibn Ubadah."
"5362","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jubarah ibn al-Mughallis narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The standard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in all battles: the standard of the Emigrants with Ali ibn Abi Talib, and the standard of the Ansar with Sad ibn Ubadah."
"5363","Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, he said: Sad ibn Ubadah died in Hawran of the land of Damascus, year sixteen."
"5364","Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, he said: Sad ibn Ubadah died two and a half years into the caliphate of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, in Hawran of the land of Syria, kunyah Abu Thabit."
"5365","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, from Ibn Awn, from Ibn Sirin, who said: While Sad urinated standing, he leaned and died; the jinn killed him, and they said: ..."
"5366","5360 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, who said: Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah stood up to urinate, then returned and said: ""I feel something in my back,"" and he did not live long after that before he died, and the jinn lamented him, saying:"
"5367","The musnad of Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him. 5361 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, and 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani, both saying: Narrated to us Isma'il ibn Abi Uways, my father narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn 'Amr ibn Shurahbil ibn Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled by an oath along with a single witness in cases of rights."
"5368","5362 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us al-Qa'nabi, (Ha) and narrated to us 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani, narrated to us Isma'il ibn Abi Uways, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman, from Isma'il ibn 'Amr ibn Qays ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from his father, that they found in the book of Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled by an oath along with a single witness, and the wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Abi Uways."
"5369","5363 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us 'Asim ibn 'Ali, narrated to us Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Take charge of the charity of the sons of so-and-so, and see to it that you do not come on the Day of Resurrection carrying a young camel on your neck or shoulder, grunting."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, turn it away from me, so he turned it away from him."
"5370","5364 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a vow that had been binding upon his mother, so he commanded him to fulfill it on her behalf."
"5371","5365 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us al-Qa'nabi, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has died with an unfulfilled vow upon her, and she did not fulfill it? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fulfill it on her behalf."""
"5372","5366 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Shu'ayb ibn Yahya al-Tujibi, (Ha) and narrated to us al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Salih, (Ha) and narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Rabi' ibn Shahin al-Basri, narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, all saying: Narrated to us al-Layth ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a vow his mother had vowed, then she died before fulfilling it? He said: ""Fulfill it on her behalf."""
"5373","5367 - Narrated to us Abu Usamah al-Halabi, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani', my grandfather narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah al-Ansari sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a vow that had been upon his mother, and she died before fulfilling it? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Fulfill it on her behalf, so that the Muslims may take it as a practice in every obligation that rests upon a person who dies before fulfilling it."""
"5374","5368 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Sulayman, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Kathir, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has died with a vow upon her; will it suffice for her if I free a slave on her behalf? He said: ""Free a slave on behalf of your mother."""
"5375","5369 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Sufyan al-Jahdari, narrated to us Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a debt owed by his mother, a slave to be freed: shall I free one on her behalf? He said: ""Yes."""
"5376","5370 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Khalid al-Massisi, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Jurayj, 'Ali ibn Muslim narrated to me, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): His mother died while he was away from her; will anything benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: ""Yes."" He said: Then I call you to witness that my fruitful orchard is charity on her behalf."
"5377","5371 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban, and 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, both saying: Narrated to us 'Abdah ibn Sulayman, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from Bakr ibn Wa'il, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother has died with an unfulfilled vow upon her which she did not fulfill, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Fulfill it on her behalf."""
"5378","5372 - Narrated to us Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, narrated to us Wahb ibn Baqiyyah, Khalid informed us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubayd Allah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah sought a ruling from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a vow that had been upon his mother, and she died before fulfilling it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fulfill it on her behalf."""
"5379","5373 - Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Janadi, narrated to us Abu Humah Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Zubaydi, narrated to us Abu Qurrah, who said: Zam'ah ibn Salih mentioned, from Ya'qub ibn 'Ata, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who informed him that Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a vow upon his mother, to fulfill it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to fulfill it on her behalf."
"5380","5374 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah, my grandfather narrated to us, Idris ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a vow that had been upon his mother, and she died before fulfilling it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled for him that he should fulfill it."
"5381","5375 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, from Musa ibn A'yan, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a debt that had been upon his mother, and she died before fulfilling it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fulfill it on her behalf."""
"5382","5376 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi, narrated to us 'Amr ibn Qust, (Ha) and narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Isma'il ibn Zurarah al-Raqqi, both saying: Narrated to us 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Amr, from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Shurahbil ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: On Friday there are five characteristics: on it Allah created Adam, and on it Adam died, and on it there is an hour in which a servant does not ask for anything but He grants it to him, so long as he does not ask for a sin or severing of kinship, and on it the Hour will be established, and there is no close angel, nor heaven, nor wind, nor mountain, but that it is apprehensive of Friday."
"5383","5377 - Narrated to us Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Harb, (Ha) and narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shumaylah, from Sa'id al-Sarraf, from Ishaq ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This clan of the Ansar is a trial: loving them is faith, and hating them is hypocrisy."
"5384","5378 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us 'Abdah ibn Sulayman, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that the mother of Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah died while he was away, and when he returned he said: O Messenger of Allah, I would like you to pray over my mother, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her grave and prayed over her, a month having passed for her."
"5385","5379 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Waki', from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has died; shall I give charity on her behalf? He said: ""Yes."" He said: Which charity is best? He said: ""Giving water to drink."""
"5386","5380 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Asbahani, narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Razi, narrated to us Abu Zuhayr 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother has died without a will and without giving charity; will it be accepted if I give charity on her behalf? He said: ""Yes."" He said: Will that benefit her? He said: ""Yes, even with a burnt sheep's trotter."""
"5387","5381 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani, narrated to us 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Sa'id ibn 'Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from his father, that his mother died while he was away, so he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: ""Yes."""
"5388","5382 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sinan, narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri, narrated to us 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Sa'id ibn 'Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the mother of Sa'd has died without a will; shall I give charity on her behalf? He said: ""Yes."""
"5389","5383 - Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Rabi' ibn Subayh, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother used to give charity and spend from my wealth during her life, and she has died; tell me, if I give charity on her behalf or free a slave on her behalf, may we hope for anything for her? He said: ""Yes."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a charity. He said: ""Give water to drink."" Al-Hasan said: The water jars of Sa'd remained in Madinah thereafter."
"5390","5384 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a charity. He said: ""Give water to drink."""
"5391","5385 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Dirar ibn Surad Abu Nu'aym al-Tahhan, narrated to us 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad, from 'Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Humayd ibn Abi al-Sa'bah, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Sa'd, shall I not guide you to a charity whose burden is light and whose reward is great? He said: Yes indeed. He said: ""Give water to drink."" So Sa'd gave water to drink."
"5392","5386 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Sahl ibn 'Uthman, narrated to us 'Abidah ibn Humayd, from Mansur, from Talhah al-Yami, from Hudhayl ibn Shurahbil, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a house, and I stood facing the door and sought permission, so he gestured to me to move away, then I came and sought permission, and he said: Is seeking permission for anything but on account of looking?"
"5393","5387 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us 'Amr ibn Marzuq, Shu'bah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Isa ibn Laqit, from a man of the people of Sham, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no one put in charge of ten but that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection shackled; nothing will release him but justice."
"5394","5388 - Narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, (Ha) and narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, both saying: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fudayl, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Isa ibn Fayid, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, may Allah have mercy on him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no commander of ten but that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection shackled; nothing will free him from his bonds but justice."
"5395","5389 - Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Khalid, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Isa ibn Fayid, from a man, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no commander of ten but that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection shackled; nothing will free him from the shackle but justice."
"5396","5390 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us 'Amr ibn Marzuq, Shu'bah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Isa ibn Laqit, from a man of the people of Sham, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no one who learns the Qur'an and then forgets it but that he will meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, leprous."
"5397","5391 - Narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, (Ha) and narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, both saying: Narrated to us Ibn Fudayl, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Isa ibn Fayid, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no one who recites the Qur'an and then forgets it but that he will meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while he is leprous."
"5398","5392 - Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Khalid, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Isa ibn Fayid, from a man, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"5399","5393 - Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, that he sought permission while facing the door, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not seek permission while facing the door."
"5400","5394 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti, narrated to us Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi, narrated to us Abu Ma'shar Najih al-Madani, narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr ibn Shurahbil ibn Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I found a man with my wife; shall I strike him with the sword? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What proof is clearer than the sword?"" Then he returned and said: ""This is the Book of our Lord."" So Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah said: O Messenger of Allah, what proof is clearer than the sword? He said: ""The Book of Allah, and a witness besides."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O company of the Ansar, this is your chief; jealousy has provoked him until he has opposed the Book of Allah."" So a man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, Sa'd is a jealous man; he never married a previously married woman out of his jealousy, and none of us could marry a woman he divorced out of his jealousy. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sa'd is jealous, and I am more jealous than him, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is more jealous than me. So a man of the Ansar said: Over what is Allah, Exalted, jealous? He said: ""He is jealous over a man striving in the path of Allah whose family is approached in his absence."""
